Cocosiri antelope enters the return season - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Xining, July 25 (Reporter Wang Jinjin) The reporter learned from the five-way beam protection station of the Cocosiri Management Office of the Yangtze River Source Park of the Sanjiangyuan National Park Administration, and the monitoring showed that the Tibetan antelopes that had previously gone to the area of Zhonai Lake in the hinterland of Cocosiri were gradually ending the production of children, and began to return to their original habitat with their cubs.
According to the monitoring screen near the five beam protection station, on July 25, about 40 female Tibetan antelopes led 3 Tibetan antelope cubs successively passed through 3002 kilometers of the Qinghai-Tibet highway and the Qinghai-Tibetan Railway, and the Tibetan antelope has begun to move back.
According to expert analysis, in recent years, the number of Tibetan antelope cubs in returning flocks accounts for one-quarter to one-fifth of the total number of Tibetan antelope flocks.
Lian Xinming, an associate researcher at the Northwest Plateau Institute of Biology of the Chinese Academy of Sciences, said: “In the early stage of relocation, Tibetan antelopes face a higher risk of arrest and food, so the number of cubs in the flock will be relatively small, and there may even be no cubs.”
According to the statistics of the Cocosiri Management Office of the Yangtze River Source Park of the Sanjiangyuan National Park Administration, the overall number of Tibetan antelope relocations has increased year by year, and the number of Tibetan antelopes in 2019 was 4,860, an increase of 338 over 2018.
Lian Ximing said: “It is expected that the return of Tibetan antelope this year will end in early September, and the number of returning Tibetan antelope is still expected to continue to increase.”
Tibetan antelopes are protected animals at the national level.
At the end of May each year, Tibetan antelopes from Qinghai Sanjiangyuan, Qiangtang in Tibet, and Arjin Mountain in Xinjiang are required to go to Lake Chonai lambs located in the hinterland of Cocosiri.
Wu Xiaomin, an expert on the protection of Tibetan antelopes in China and a researcher at the Shaanxi Zoological Research Institute (Northwest Institute of Endangered Animals), said: "Tibetan antelopes are the process of returning to their habitats with cubs after the return of female Tibetan antelopes. At first, the return groups that left the place of birth are relatively large, but then Tibetan antelopes will return to their respective habitats according to different geographical populations and along different paths."
In order to ensure the safe relocation of Tibetan antelope flocks, the reporter learned that a few days ago, the Cocosiri Management Office of the Yangtze River Source Park of the Sanjiangyuan National Park has arranged for staff to continue to carry out video monitoring and jurisdiction patrols in the main relocation area.
If it is found that there is a Tibetan antelope sheep trying to cross the road, the mountain rangers will carry out temporary traffic control in the first time, so that the sheep can safely pass through the wildlife channel, and ensure that they are as less affected by human interference during the relocation.
So, how to solve the heat in daily life?
Experts suggest that when going out in the summer as much as possible, it is best not to walk or work in the hot sun around noon, because the sunshine of this time period is the strongest, and the possibility of heat stroke is higher.
If you must go out at this time, you must do a good job of protection, such as wearing umbrellas, wearing sun hats, wearing sunglasses, and the best sunscreen with conditions to prevent sunburn.
As far as possible, the clothes use light-coloured, well-permeasible cotton, hemp and silk textures, and wear less chemical fiber clothing, so as not to be unable to dissipate heat in time when sweating a lot, resulting in heat stroke.
In hot and hot weather, be prepared to drink plenty of water, drink in time, don't wait until you're thirsty to drink water, because once you feel thirsty that your body is already short of water, every time you drink water is controlled at 150 ml to 200 ml, drink warm water, and don't drink ice water.
Depending on the temperature, the general staff drank 1.5 to 2 liters of water per day, and the high-temperature workers drank 3 to 5 liters of water per day.
When sweating more, you can properly add some salt water to make up for the salt lost by the human body due to sweating.
In addition, in the summer, the human body is prone to lack of potassium, which makes people feel tired and tired, and containing potassium tea is an excellent summer drink.
In the summer, eat more fruits and vegetables with high water content, such as lettuce, cucumbers, tomatoes, etc.; fresh fruits, such as peaches, almonds, watermelons, melons, etc., have a moisture content of 80% to 90%, which can be used to add water; dairy products can not only replenish water, but also meet the nutritional needs of the body.
In addition, people who work in high-temperature environments should be properly supplemented with drinks that contain elements such as potassium and magnesium.
In summer, the days and nights are short, the temperature is high, the human metabolism is vigorous, the consumption is also large, and it is easy to feel fatigue.
Adequate sleep can relax all systems of the brain and body, which is conducive to work and study, and it is also a measure to prevent heat stroke.
According to experts, the best time to sleep is from 22:00 to 23:00, and the best time to wake up is from 5:30 to 6:30 p.m.
When sleeping, be careful not to lie under the air conditioning outlet and electric fan, so as not to suffer from air conditioning disease and fever.
Experts suggest that in the outdoor activities or high-temperature operations of the people, you can carry ten drops of water, dane, fragrant positive air water or garlic positive gas pills and other anti-heat drugs, or placed in the nearest workplace, at any time to use, in order to prevent the occurrence of heat stroke.
Graduate art exhibition moved into the mall public welfare exhibition-Xinhua.com
In the "cloud graduation" season of major colleges and universities, a rare offline graduate art exhibition opened warmly last weekend.
However, it is neither in the museum nor on the campus, but it appears in the public space of Chaoyang Dayue City, and is open to the public for free and will continue until August 23.
The reporter learned that the 2020 graduate art exhibition collected 50 pieces/group of works by 57 young artists from the Central Academy of Fine Arts, China Communication University and Tianjin Academy of Fine Arts, and the exhibition space was extended from the 2nd floor to the 6th floor, and made full use of the flat works displayed by the lantern box in the building to maximize the artistic atmosphere of the graduation season.
Under the epidemic, the significance of this exhibition is particularly special.
Chaoyang Dayue City Mei Chen responsible person Ge flat said: "We choose to go to the 'cloud' graduation exhibition once again brought back to the offline space, but also hope to let more people see young people's exploration of themselves and their understanding of the world, magnifying the healing power of art for society and the soul."
She revealed that the works participating in the exhibition were solicited from the graduates of several major art colleges and universities, and selected suitable for commercial space display, and the forms of the works ranged from traditional stand paintings, sculptures, to new media installations, interactive animations, VR panoramas, and the volume and richness were among the best in the past years.
Among them, Li Yunxiao expressed his feelings in this epidemic through a mixture of mechanical and handmade creative language in the "first battle of 2020"; Liu Jiaying's work "Sound Money" created through the Ethereum blockchain explored the themes of "cryptocurrencies", "credit creation", "transactions" and so on; Zhang Jiaqi's "Cat Forest" and Qiu Daqiang's "Fetter" are often accompanied by human animals, from which young artists can see their understanding of the relationship between people and animals.
Among the few graduates who personally arranged the exhibition, there was Li Jingyin from the Sculpture Department of the Tianjin Academy of Fine Arts.
"I came to Beijing on July 7, when I was actually a little worried about the epidemic, but also three days in advance of nucleic acid testing, with alcohol cotton and test reports to show."
The structure of his work "Yesterday as a Mystery" is more complex and must be done personally.
At the same time, he also undertakes the task of helping his classmates repair damaged works.
"The exhibition until 4:30 a.m., and then to repair, the time is very tight, forgot to take a picture with the work, but also a little regret."
He hopes that when the epidemic is more stable, he will come to Beijing with his classmates to see his work exhibition.
