In the same morning, 65-year-old Bolsonaro tweeted a photo of him wearing sneakers, not wearing a mask, sitting at a table for breakfast, with a smile on his face, thumbs up in one hand and a box of hydroxychloroquine in the other.
He tweeted: “Good morning everyone, the new coronavirus test results: negative.”
However, Bolsonaro did not say when the test of the new coronavirus turned negative was carried out.
On July 5, Bolsonaro developed symptoms of new crown pneumonia, received positive virus test results on the 6th, and on the 7th, he claimed to have been diagnosed with new crown pneumonia through live television on the 7th.
On the 14th and 21st, Bolsonaro tested for the new coronavirus twice, and the results were still positive.
During the isolation period, Bolsonaro showed the hydroxychloroquine drugs he was taking many times through social media and said that hydroxychloroquine had a very good effect on the new crown pneumonia and felt good after taking it, thanks to hydroxychloroquine in good physical condition, and advocated that Brazilian medical institutions use hydroxychloroquine for the treatment of new crown pneumonia.
According to Brazilian media reports, as of now, there are five cabinet ministers and 10 governors in Brazil who have been diagnosed with new crown pneumonia.
A small plane crashed in the Swiss Alps, and all four people on board were killed.
According to the European Network quoted by the European Union News Agency, on July 25 local time, the Swiss police informed the media that a small plane crashed in the Swiss Alps on the 25th.
All two Swiss and two Austrians on board were killed in the accident.
According to reports, a police statement in the southern Swiss canton of Wallis said that a small plane crashed more than 3,000 meters above sea level near the Alpine peak in the canton of Valais, and rescuers rushed to the crash site to confirm that all four people on board the plane were killed.
Valais state police said that witnesses called police at 12:25 p.m. on the 25th, saying that he had witnessed a small plane falling from the sky.
A few minutes later, witnesses again informed the police that there had been heavy smoke at the crash site.
After receiving the alarm, the police quickly coordinated fire officers, medical staff and rescue workers and carried helicopters to the scene of the accident.
When rescuers arrived at the crash site, they found that all four people on board had been killed.
Police confirmed that the victims of the accident included two Swiss, aged 50 and 66, as well as two Austrians aged 46 and 50.
At present, police are working with the Swiss Transport Safety Commission to jointly investigate the cause of the crash, police said.
Heavy rain in 33 districts and counties in Chongqing issued a yellow and orange flood warning
Chongqing, July 26 (Reporter Liu Xianglin) The reporter learned from the Chongqing Municipal Water Conservancy Bureau on the 26th that in the past 24 hours, there have been heavy rains in 33 districts and counties in Chongqing, of which 16 districts and counties have heavy rains.
Heavy rains have caused 71 small and medium-sized rivers in Chongqing to rise, and two flood warnings have been issued.
According to the monitoring of the Chongqing Hydrological Monitoring Station, from 8 o'clock on the 25th to 8 o'clock on the 26th, there were heavy rains in most parts of Chongqing, and heavy rains in localities.
There have been heavy rains in 33 districts and counties such as Tongnan, Tongliang and Hechuan, among which heavy rains have occurred in 16 districts and counties such as Zhongxian, Kaizhou and Wuxi; the maximum daily rainfall occurred in Longshan Village, Jinshan Town, Nanchuan, with 197.5 mm.
71 small and medium-sized rivers such as Lianjiang, Qiongjiang and Kaizhou South River have a rise of 1 to 7 meters, and the highest water level has not exceeded the alert water level.
It is expected that from 8 o'clock on the 26th to 8 o'clock on the 27th, small and medium-sized rivers in most parts of Chongqing may have different degrees of rising water, and some small and medium-sized rivers may have excessive water level floods.
At the same time, we will also pay attention to the possible transit floods of the Yangtze River and the Jialing River.
