During watching the game, spectators must wear masks throughout the process, enter the number, and strictly maintain an interval of one meter.
When exiting, the audience must maintain an orderly withdrawal of the "one-meter line" social distance in accordance with the order of the backward forward, the first two sides and then the middle.
Xinjiang deep ploughing "sunflower field" with good clean energy - Sino-New Network
2020-07-26 15:43:42 Source: China News Network Author: Chen Haifeng Responsibility Editor: Chen Haifeng
Xinhua News Agency, Xinjiang Hami, July 26th: Xinjiang deeply cultivates the "Sunflower field" with good clean energy
More than 6,000 pentagonal heliostats, 48 square meters each, arranged neatly in a circle, such as a piece of silver "sunflower field", rotating with the sun, reflecting sunlight into the center of more than 200 meters high heat-absorbing tower, to achieve power generation.
On the 25th, the reporter saw this scene at the Hami molten salt tower-type solar-thermal power generation site in Yiwu County, Hami City, Xinjiang.
"The so-called molten salt tower-type solar thermal power generation is to reflect the sunlight through the mirror to the heat-absorbing tower to form thermal energy, and then through the traditional power generation technology to convert heat energy into electricity."
Zhang Yong, deputy general manager of CNC Hami Solar Thermal Power Generation Co., Ltd., said that its design principle is similar to the solar stove used in the rural areas of northwestern China, and the sunlight should be gathered together.
Construction of the farm began in October 2017 and was connected to the grid at the end of last year, covering an area of 6,600 acres, with a total of 14,500 fixed mirrors planned to be installed.
“Compared to traditional solar power generation technology, its biggest advantage is that it can store concentrated thermal energy and generate electricity at night.”
Zhang Yong said that the 13-hour heat storage system configured by the project can keep the generator unit running continuously and steadily, not affected by light changes; it can also quickly participate in the peaking of the power grid according to the demand of the power grid.
After the project is fully completed, it can achieve an annual power generation of 198 million degrees, save more than 60,000 tons of standard coal per year, reduce more than 60 tons of sulfur dioxide, more than 60 tons of nitrogen oxides, about 20 tons of soot, more than 150,000 tons of carbon dioxide, and provide a steady stream of clean energy for the locality.
In addition, there is another piece of silver "Sunflower Field" in Shichengzi Photovoltaic Industrial Park in Hami City.
Hamifer Solar Photovoltaic Power Station covers an area of more than 2,300 acres, and 714 power generation equipment that has been built also follow the rotation of the sun, and always maintains a 90-degree right angle of sunlight and concentrated panel.
“We use two-axis tracking concentrated power generation technology, and through unified integrated control, all power generation equipment will adjust the angle according to the solar height to maintain power generation efficiency.”
The power station manager said that under the conditions of good light weather, the power generation technology can be increased by about 20% compared with the traditional photovoltaic power generation efficiency.
In the first half of this year, the power station has achieved more than 7 million degrees of power generation, supplementing the local electricity demand.
Shichenzi Photovoltaic Industrial Park is currently the largest monomer in Xinjiang and the most complete photovoltaic industry demonstration park for photovoltaic modules, with a total of 38 photovoltaic power generation projects, with a total installed capacity of 820,000 kilowatts.
In the first half of this year, the power generation completed exceeded 110 million degrees, an increase of 6% over the same period in 2019.
Hami is one of the regions with the best conditions for solar energy resources in China.
The average annual total solar radiation volume is more than 6,200 megajoules per square meter, and about 3,200 hours of sunshine throughout the year.
In recent years, the city has vigorously developed the photovoltaic industry and planted a good "sunflower field".
It has been installed more than 2.5 million kilowatts of solar power generation scale, in the first half of this year, the city's photovoltaic power generation exceeded 1.4 billion degrees, an increase of about 14%.
At present, there are more than 330 grid-connected photovoltaic power plants in Xinjiang, with an installed capacity of more than 10 million kilowatts.
It is expected that the annual photovoltaic power generation will reach 15 billion degrees this year, which can replace more than 6 million tons of standard coal.
The police reported that the details of "female college students going to Qinghai tourism lost contact" search and rescue work continues - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Xining, July 26 (Reporter Wang Jinjin Zhou Zhe) Recently, "a female college student lost contact after traveling to Qinghai Golmud" caused netizens to pay attention.
Qinghai Province Haixi Mongolian Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture Germu City Public Security Bureau reported on the 26th that a university student in Nanjing Huang is still in a state of loss of contact, and the police in many places are going deep into the missing area of Huang and actively carrying out the search for work.
On July 10, 2020, the public security detachment of the Germu City Public Security Bureau of Haixi Prefecture was notified by its superiors that a university student in Nanjing took the Z164 train from Nanjing to Germu on July 5, and on July 9 in the southwestern area of Qingshui River Protection Station in Qumao County, Yushu Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture, Qinghai Province.
According to the investigation of the Golmud City Public Security Bureau, Huang entered the territory of Qinghai Province at 19:54 on July 6 and arrived in Golmud City at 4:00 on the 7th.
At 8 o'clock on the same day, the missing person Huang Moumou took a taxi from the Golmud City Yellow River Hotel towards the G109 National Road, and arrived at 12 o'clock at the Coco Siri Sonandaj protection station, the taxi driver returned alone, Huang arrived at 15 o'clock on the 7th arrived at the Qingshui River area near the Sonam Daj protection station until 16:00 on the 9th to shut down in the area.
In a further investigation, the police found that Huang had passed through the Najigou checkpoint at 17:07 on July 13.
Naiqou checkpoint is a checkpoint set up by Naqu City, Tibet Autonomous Region, in Nanshankou, Golmud City, because there is no video surveillance at the checkpoint, it is impossible to determine the information of myself and the vehicle, the police can only drive along the way to look up, to coordinate the checkpoints along the way in Tibet if found Huang, immediately contacted the Golmud City Public Security Bureau.
According to the latest situation, at 1 a.m. on July 26, the Golmud City Public Security Bureau organized rescue forces to carry rescue equipment, went to the non-freezing spring protection station along the Qinghai-Tibet highway, Sonandaj protection station, and actively contacted the Sichuan police, the Tibetan police, and the Nanjing police to work together.
The local police hope that the majority of netizens and all sectors of society if there are relevant clues, in a timely manner to the Golmud police and Nanjing Jiangning police, and strive to find the lost contact person Huang Moumou as soon as possible.
At the same time, the relevant experts suggest that tourists should be standardized, rational and civilized in outdoor activities, always pay attention to roadside warning signs, do not venture into no-man's land, encounter unexpected situations, and call the police in time.
U.S. media reveals the truth that the U.S. has unwarrantedly asked China to close its consulate in Houston
2020-07-26 14:40:44 Source: CCTV Author: Zhu Yanjing Responsibility Editor: Zhu Yanjing
U.S. media reveal the truth about U.S. unwarranted demands that China close its consulate in Houston
On the 24th, the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs informed the U.S. Embassy in China that China decided to revoke the establishment and operation of the U.S. Consulate General in Chengdu, and put forward specific requests to stop all business and activities of the Consulate General, as a counter-measure by the U.S. side suddenly asking China to close its consulate in Houston on the 21st.
The U.S. government's behavior has aroused a lot of attention, and its political motivation has been questioned by foreign media and scholars.
Whahy do you ask China to close its Consulate General?
A number of foreign media said that it is not clear why the United States will choose the Chinese Consulate General in Houston, but for the purpose of this move, foreign media bluntly said: for the election.
CNN reported on the 23rd that the United States asked China to close its consulate general in Houston, causing people to question their political motivations.
According to the article, the U.S. government's disastrous response to the new crown epidemic has caused President Donald Trump's pre-electoral polling support rate to be relatively sluggish.
White House officials privately said that the tough strategy taken against China is to save Trump's approval rating, but also to divert responsibility for the White House's failed response to the epidemic.
According to the article, China's Consulate General in Houston is a "politic-driven, very cautious" goal chosen by the United States, and the U.S. government chose it "in order to create a tough attitude, while avoiding the risk of causing major conflicts."
The British Broadcasting Corporation (BBC) also believes that when the U.S. election season is approaching and the U.S. economy has been hit hard by the epidemic, Trump believes that "playing the 'China card' has political advantages."
The current situation is "a spiraling, tit-for-tat struggle", driven in part by the U.S. government from the perspective of domestic considerations, and will only worsen tensions between China and the United States.
CBS reported that Trump's re-election prospects were under pressure due to the outbreak, and he repeatedly blamed China because of the epidemic.
Almost every day in the United States, there are new actions against Trump’s so-called “Chinese exploitation of the United States.”
“The Consulate General of Houston is very important in establishing ties between the two countries.”
U.S. calls for China to close its consulate in Houston have heightened tensions between the world’s two largest economies.
If the Chinese Consulate General in Houston is closed, in addition to the diplomatic influence, Chinese citizens in the southern United States face difficulties in obtaining consular services, and U.S. citizens seeking visas and other services also face difficulties.
A business group in Houston expressed regret that the United States had asked China to close its consulate in Houston, saying that it played an important role in establishing trade, investment and cultural ties between the two countries.
The Associated Press believes that this reflects the importance of China's economy.
According to the foreign policy magazine website, the U.S. move "is part of a series of provocative measures that will only worsen U.S.-China relations."
Jonathan Pollack, an expert on East Asia at the Brookings Institution, said that since the establishment of full diplomatic relations between the United States and China in 1979, he could not think of any action comparable to the U.S. operation against the Chinese Consulate General in Houston.
Hong Kong's "South China Morning Post" reported that this move by the United States is unprecedented in more than 40 years of diplomatic relations between China and the United States.
Analysts believe that this move may cause lasting damage.
The Chinese Consulate General in Houston was built in 1979 and was the first Chinese Consulate General opened in the United States.
At present, China has an embassy in the United States and five consulates-general.
Russia held a military parade to celebrate the Navy Festival - Xinhua
On July 26, in St. Petersburg, Russia, ships lined up to participate in the Navy Day celebrations.
Xinhua News Agency (photo by Mojina)
MOSCOW, July 26 (Xinhua) -- Russia's various fleets held a military parade on July 26 to celebrate the Navy's 324th anniversary.
On the same day, the Russian North Sea, the Baltic Sea, the Black Sea, the Caspian Sea and the Pacific Fleet held military parades in the waters where their respective bases are located, with a total of 15,000 soldiers, 219 ships of various types and 71 military aircraft participating.
The President of the Russian Federation, the supreme commander of the armed forces, Putin, attended the military parade of the Baltic Fleet.
About 4,000 soldiers, 46 ships and more than 40 warplanes participated in the local military parade.
Putin first inspected the line-up of ships in the waters of his naval base in Kronstadt, Baltic.
Later, in a speedboat, he reached the waters of the Neva River in the center of St. Petersburg and went ashore to watch the military parade held on the Neva River.
Speaking at the military parade, Putin said that the level of modernization technology of Russian naval equipment has continued to improve in recent years, and the Russian Navy will receive a total of about 40 new ships equipped with unique hypersonic strike systems in 2020.
In addition, the commander-in-chief of the Russian Navy Yevmenov recently said in an interview with the Russian Ministry of Defense that Russia's plans to build ships have been effectively implemented, and the number of new ships that the Russian Navy plans to receive in 2020 is a large scale in recent years.
In 1696, Tsar Peter the Great began to form a maritime fleet, creating the history of the Russian Navy.
The last Sunday in July is the Russian Navy’s Day.
