National Health and Health Commission: 46 new confirmed cases on July 25 and 22 cases in Liaoning in Xinjiang - Economic Observer
According to the National Health Commission, from 0 to 24:00 on July 25, 31 provinces (autonomous regions and municipalities directly under the Central Government) and the Xinjiang Production and Construction Corps reported 46 new confirmed cases, of which 11 cases were imported from abroad (5 cases in Inner Mongolia, 3 cases in Guangdong, 1 case in Tianjin, 1 case in Fujian and 1 case in Shandong), 35 local cases (22 cases in Xinjiang and 13 cases in Liaoning); no new deaths; 2 new suspected cases, all of which were imported cases from abroad.
On the same day, 19 new cases were cured and discharged from the hospital, 673 close contacts were released from medical observation, and the number of severe cases increased by 7 from the previous day.
There are 82 confirmed cases (including 2 severe cases) and 3 suspected cases.
The total number of confirmed cases was 2,045, the total number of cured discharged cases was 1963, and there were no deaths.
As of 24:00 on July 25, according to the reports of 31 provinces (autonomous regions and municipalities directly under the Central Government) and the Xinjiang Production and Construction Corps, there are 288 confirmed cases (including 18 severe cases), a total of 78,908 discharged cases, a total of 4634 deaths, a total of 83,830 confirmed cases, and 3 suspected cases.
A total of 779,000 close contacts have been traced, and 11,762 close contacts are still under medical observation.
31 provinces (autonomous regions and municipalities directly under the Central Government) and the Xinjiang Production and Construction Corps reported 68 new cases of asymptomatic infection (8 cases imported from abroad); 17 cases were converted to confirmed cases on the same day (no overseas input); 10 cases of medical observation were lifted on the same day (7 cases imported from abroad); 292 cases of asymptomatic infection were still under medical observation (91 cases imported from abroad).
A total of 3009 confirmed cases have been reported from Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan.
Among them, there were 2505 cases in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (1,455 discharges and 18 deaths), 46 cases in the Macao Special Administrative Region (46 discharges) and 458 cases (440 discharges and 7 deaths).
The longest high-speed rail tunnel in the Three Gorges Reservoir District - Sino-Singapore Network
2020-07-26 17:34:48 Source: China News Network Author: Chen Haifeng Responsibility Editor: Chen Haifeng
Pictured is the construction site of the Three Gorges Tunnel.
China Railway Chengdu Bureau Group Co., Ltd.
Zhongxin network Chongqing July 26th (Reporter Han Lu) reporter from China Railway Chengdu Bureau Group Co., Ltd. was informed on the 26th, the total length of about 18.9 kilometers of Zhengwan high-speed rail small Three Gorges tunnel through the whole line.
It is understood that the Little Three Gorges Tunnel is not only the longest high-speed rail tunnel in the Three Gorges Repository Area, but also the longest single-hole two-line high-speed rail tunnel that is currently under construction in China.
Zhengwan high-speed rail is located in Henan, Hubei, Chongqing three provinces and cities, in Zhengzhou north to Beijing, Xulan high-speed rail, in Wanzhou South Lianyuwan high-speed rail arrived in Chongqing, is China's "eight vertical and eight horizontal" high-speed rail network along the river channel and Hunan channel is an important part.
Zhengwan high-speed rail small Three Gorges tunnel 26 days through the whole line.
Pictured through the scene.
Zhengwan high-speed rail began in Zhengzhou City, Henan Province, to the southwest through Pingdingshan City, Nanyang City, Hubei Province Xiangyang City to Chongqing Wanzhou District, the new line length of about 818 kilometers, the design speed of 350 km / h, about 184 kilometers in Chongqing.
Among them, the Zhengzhou to Xiangyang section has been opened for operation on December 1, 2019, and the Chongqing section is stepping up construction.
On the 26th, the small Three Gorges Tunnel passed through the whole line was the control project of the Zhengwan high-speed railway, and the project was located at the border between Fengjie County and Wushan County in Chongqing, with a total length of about 18.9 kilometers and a maximum depth of 890 meters.
Construction of the tunnel began in February 2017 and passed through on July 26, 2020.
According to the investigation and design of China Railway Second Academy of Engineering Group Co., Ltd. Zhengwan high-speed rail tunnel design person in charge of the Royal Army, the small Three Gorges Tunnel is located in the location of the terrain geological conditions are very complex, facing the risk of karst, sudden mud water, soft rock deformation, etc., belongs to the I high-risk tunnel, the tunnel design and construction is extremely difficult.
"During the construction of the project, we used geological survey methods, object detection methods, and advanced drilling methods to advance geological forecasting, and adopted special design solutions for more than 30 types of caverns. For example, a 24-meter-long bridge was designed and built, and a large cavern with a vertical length of more than 10 meters and a depth of more than 55 meters across the tunnel, so as to avoid the sinking of the tunnel," the Royal Army said.
According to the China Railway Tunnel Bureau of the construction side, when the construction of the tunnel is carried out, it adopts the combination of dredging and blocking, through the construction of cross-hole flat guide, slue filling, the strengthening of tunnel structure support and the construction of sewage treatment stations, which not only ensures the orderly advancement of the project, but also avoids the damage of the construction and drainage to the water body of the small Three Gorges Scenic Area, while successfully overcoming the construction problems such as bad geology such as the large deformation of 7 kilometers of soft rock, and the maximum daily surging water.
After the completion of the Zhengwan high-speed rail line, it will become a new convenient and fast passenger channel in the southwestern region of China to the Central Plains, North China and Northeast China, which is of great significance for improving the capacity and quality of the north-east-to-northeast railway channel in the southwest region, improving the layout of the regional road network, accelerating the development of tourism resources along the route, promoting regional coordinated development, and promoting the implementation of the western development strategy.
Experts say collecting immigration data through U.S. Census for House seat allocation is unconstitutional
Some civil rights groups and several U.S. cities and counties have sued the U.S. federal government, saying Trump’s presidency’s attempts to exclude undocumented immigrants from the U.S. Census would not be feasible and unconstitutional.
The U.S. Census will determine the allocation of seats in the U.S. House of Representatives.
Sarah Brannon, executive counsel of the American Civil Liberties Union, told VOA that “it doesn’t work.”
She went on to say that it would be difficult and “not very reliable” for Trump to ask for the citizenship of those who accept the census to be determined in the census.
Another civil liberties organization, a common cause group, filed a lawsuit Thursday challenging Trump’s executive order.
Some cities in New Jersey and Georgia joined the lawsuit.
Arlington County in Virginia also joined the lawsuit Friday.
“The U.S. Constitution requires an accurate account of our population every 10 years. We must take an accurate account of everyone living in Arlington County, and we will not allow this illegal attempt to frighten and reduce the number of people in our immigrant communities.”
Other organizations and individuals praised President Trump's executive order.
Alabama Attorney General Marshall called the executive order a “victory” for the state.
He said that “the allocation of seats in the House of Representatives of the Länders and seats of the Electoral College must be based on the number of residents living in the Länder and the number of residents legally residing.”
The U.S. Supreme Court last year prevented the Trump administration from including citizenship issues in its 2020 census table.
Earlier this week, President Trump signed an executive order that would oversee the U.S. Census Bureau’s Commerce Secretary, Ross, by submitting data on the unlicensed population from the census, so that the administration can exclude these unlicensed populations from each state’s census numbers, and to determine whether each state is increasing or decreasing or maintaining a House of Representatives seat.
The U.S. has to redistribute seats in the House of Representatives every 10 years based on demographic changes.
33 districts and counties in Chongqing torrential rains Locally launched flood control level IV emergency response-Zhongxin.com
Xinhua News Agency, Chongqing, July 26 (Reporter Ke Gaoyang, Li Song) The reporter learned from the Chongqing flood control and drought relief headquarters that Chongqing has ushered in a new round of heavy rainfall from July 25, 33 districts and counties have heavy rain, 4 small and medium-sized rivers have experienced ultra-alert water level floods, and the local government has launched a flood control level IV emergency response.
According to the monitoring of Chongqing Hydrological Monitoring Station, from 8 o'clock on the 25th to 8 o'clock on the 26th, most parts of Chongqing ushered in heavy rains, and heavy rains occurred in 33 districts and counties such as Jiangjin, Qijiang and Wulong, among which 16 districts and counties such as Wanzhou, Yunyang and Nanchuan experienced heavy rains.
The largest daily rainfall occurred in Longshan Village, Jinshan Town, Nanchuan, at 197.5 mm.
Affected by heavy rainfall, four small and medium-sized rivers in Jiangjin District, Donkey Creek, Fuling District, Yingyang River in Kaizhou District, and Yunyang County, there were ultra-alert water level floods, and the current water level is still rising.
The heavy rainfall also led to landslides in Liujing Village in Wulong District Land Township, resulting in the interruption of the passage of village roads, and the slippery slope into the Wujiang tributaries along the Cang River, blocking the formation of the river to form a lake, and the local authorities have urgently organized the transfer of the downstream masses.
In response to the rainstorm, the Chongqing flood control and drought relief headquarters issued river flood level III warning information at 13:00 on the 26th, and launched flood control level IV emergency response, requiring relevant districts, counties and units to strengthen inspections, timely mobilization of emergency rescue teams and materials, and evacuating and transferring the people in threatened areas.
