Moroccan naviar intercepts cannabis products in Mediterranean
Rabat, July 26 (Reporter Chen Binjie) According to Moroccan media reports on the 26th, the coast guard belonging to the Moroccan Navy intercepted a batch of cannabis products in the Mediterranean on the same day, with a total weight of more than 1 ton.
Morocco's official news agency quoted military sources as saying that the Moroccan coast guard intercepted a speedboat suspected of smuggling cannabis products while patrolling in the Mediterranean on the same day, and the suspect threw the cannabis products from the ship into the sea before being arrested, and the coast guard then picked it up.
