Tunisia's president nominates new prime minister - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Tunisia, July 25 (Reporter Huang Ling) Tunisia's presidential office issued an announcement on the 25th, saying that President Saeed nominated Hisham Mehihi, the interior minister of the caretaker's government, as the new prime minister on the same day.
According to the constitution, Maishihi should complete the formation of the government within one month and submit the list of the composition of the new government to Parliament for approval.
The formation of the new government must be approved by more than half of the 217 members of Parliament.
He was born in 1974 with a master’s degree in law and management, and in February this year he was appointed Minister of the Interior.
On July 15, then-Tunisian Prime Minister Fahfah offered his resignation, which was approved by the president.
Earlier, Tunisia's largest party in Tunisia's parliament announced the withdrawal of support for Fahfah's government, resulting in a lack of sufficient support in parliament.
The overall stability of employment and prices shows that the economy has a "temperature"
2020-07-26 07:01:37 Source: Economic Daily Author:Wang Sisuo Responsibility Editor:Wang Sisuo
The overall stability of employment and prices shows that the economy has "temperature"
Economic Daily · China Economic Net reporter Lin Zhencan
In the first half of this year, in the face of the impact of the new crown pneumonia epidemic, China's overall efforts to promote epidemic prevention and control and economic and social development, the epidemic prevention and control situation continues to improve, the steady recovery of the economy is obvious, the employment and price performance closely related to people's livelihood are generally stable, and China's economy has handed over a temperature economic operation report card.
In the first two months of this year, the survey unemployment rate increased.
Especially in February, the production and business activities of many enterprises were basically shut down, the demand for employment of enterprises was reduced, recruitment was delayed or cancelled, and the unemployment rate in urban surveys increased.
With the gradual improvement of the epidemic prevention and control situation, the order of production and life of the whole society has been continuously restored.
The Party Central Committee adheres to the general tone of steady progress, further increases macro policy hedging efforts, comprehensively strengthens employment priority policies, and actively promotes the work of stabilizing jobs and expanding employment.
China has increased its policies to hedge and stabilize jobs, played a combination of "reduced and reduced rebates" policy, reduced the payment part of 3 social insurance units in stages, allowed to delay the payment of social insurance premiums, expanded the steady return of unemployment insurance for small and medium-sized micro-enterprises, benefited from the work-for-training policy, and absorbed subsidies and apprenticeship subsidies for the employment of key groups of enterprises.
With the implementation of various stable employment policies, the demand for employment of enterprises has steadily rebounded, the employment situation has gradually improved, the unemployment rate of urban surveys has gradually declined, and in June, the survey unemployment rate was 5.7%.
Zhang Yi, director of the Population and Employment Statistics Department of the National Bureau of Statistics, said that in the second quarter, various employment policies continued to be effective, and the labor force that withdrew due to the impact of the epidemic returned in the early period, and the urban labor participation rate in June increased by about 10 percentage points compared with February, which was close to the level of the same period last year.
According to the data, the total number of urban employment in June increased by more than 19% compared with February, and most industries reached the pre-epidemic level; the average weekly working hours of enterprise employees reached 46.8 hours, an increase of 6.6 hours compared with February and 0.1 hours higher than in January.
Prices are also related to thousands of households.
In January this year, the CPI increased by 5.4% year-on-year, hitting a new high in many years.
Entering February, although the year-on-year increase of CPI fell slightly, it is still in the "5 range".
CPI year-on-year growth is at a high level, both before the Spring Festival consumer demand driving factors, as well as the Spring Festival wrong month and year-on-year base lower factors.
However, the impact of the new crown pneumonia epidemic on prices is particularly obvious.
Affected by the prevention and control of the epidemic, in January and February, there were delays in logistics throughout the country, the supply of materials was not timely, the cost of material transportation increased, etc., coupled with some citizens hoarding and buying, the price of some daily necessities increased significantly.
In order to cope with the disturbance caused by the prevention and control of the epidemic on the price situation, the relevant departments have included important living materials in the scope of emergency transportation security to ensure the smooth transportation of materials.
Under the influence of a series of policy measures, the supply of vegetable melon and fruit market has been strongly guaranteed.
In order to cope with the rapid rise in pork prices at the beginning of this year, after the central government introduced a policy to ensure price stability, all regions and departments quickly implemented it, the supply of pork reserves was significantly improved, pig production capacity was restored in an orderly manner, and the order of production and sales was gradually normal.
Since March, pork prices have declined continuously, driving the year-on-year increase in food prices to 10.6% in May; in June, pork prices rose slightly month-on-month due to factors such as the slowdown in the release of pigs, the reduction of imports and the recovery of group consumer demand.
Seasonal changes in fresh vegetable prices are obvious, rising by an average of 3.4% in the first half of the year.
Affected by the higher comparative base of the same period last year, fresh fruit prices continued to decline year-on-year, with an average decline of 13.3% in the first half of the year
The basic life of the masses has been effectively guaranteed, and the overall economic and social situation has been stable and orderly.
With the gradual recovery of transportation and logistics, all localities have increased their supply and security efforts, and the supply and demand situation in the market has improved.
At the beginning of March, the CPI fell for four consecutive months, and the year-on-year increase also fell from 4.3% in March to 2.5% in June, and the overall price level recovered steadily.
In the second half of the year, China's prices will continue to maintain a moderate level, and the overall inflationary pressure is small, but it is still necessary to promote the restoration of production and life order under the premise of normalizing epidemic prevention and control.
Effectively respond to natural disasters such as floods and droughts in the main producing areas of agricultural products such as food, fruits and vegetables, strengthen market supervision, and resolutely crack down on acts such as hoarding and raising prices to disrupt market order.
