Greenland opens a new round of mixed reform Shanghai state-owned enterprises to transfer 17.5% of shares - Economic Observer - Professional financial news website
On July 26, Greenland Holdings (600606.SH) issued the "Indicative Announcement on State-owned Shareholders' Plans to Transfer Some Shares and Resumption of the Company's Shares and Resumptions through the Public Collection of Transferees."
According to the content of the announcement, in order to further deepen the reform of state-owned state-owned enterprises, optimize the restructuring of state-owned enterprises, and improve the shareholding structure of green space, Shanghai Real Estate (Group) Co., Ltd. (hereinafter referred to as "Shanghai Real Estate") and Shanghai City Investment (Group) Co., Ltd. (hereinafter referred to as "Shanghai City Investment") intend to transfer some of the company's shares held through an open solicitation of transferees.
The price of the shares to be transferred this time is not lower than the arithmetic average of the daily weighted average price for the first 30 trading days of the indicative announcement date (July 27, 2020); the audited net asset value of the company in the most recent fiscal year.
At present, the new strategic investors in the green area are still inconclusive, according to the announcement information estimates, the new strategic investors want to win the 17.5 percent of the shares transferred in the mixed reform of the greenfield needs to pay about 14 billion yuan of funds.
It is worth noting that after the completion of this share transfer, it is expected that there will still be no controlling shareholders and actual controllers in Greenland, but the control structure may change greatly.
Since its establishment, Greenland Holdings has carried out a number of institutional reforms: from 1992 to 1997, it operated in accordance with market-oriented rules under the purely state-owned system; from 1997 to 2013, it established and continuously improved the joint-stock system of state-owned holding and employee shareholding; in 2013-2015, strategic investors were introduced to form a mixed ownership system of state-owned and non-public capital cross-shareholding and mutual integration; since 2015, the overall listing has become a public company.
Greenland's current mixed reform plan is similar to Gree, in December 2019, Gaolu Capital led Zhuhai Mingjun to take over 15% of Gree Electric Appliances (000651.SZ) for 41.662 billion yuan, Gree Group retired to minority shareholders, after the completion of the mixed reform, Gree Electrical Appliances implemented an executive incentive plan, no actual controller structure and other modern enterprise management methods.
Shanghai real estate, Shanghai City Investment are all wholly-owned by the State-owned enterprise group held by the State-owned Assets Supervision and Administration Commission of Shanghai, Zhang Yuliang, chairman and president of Greenland Holdings, said that the green space is an important measure for Shanghai to promote the comprehensive reform of state-owned state-owned enterprises in accordance with the requirements of the Party Central Committee and accelerate the reform of state-owned state-owned enterprises in a new stage, fully demonstrating the new ideas of local conditions and tailor-to-wear, by introducing new outstanding strategic shareholders to listed companies.
Cross-provincial travel recovery The country's first inter-provincial EMU tourism train - Xinhua
HANGZHOU, July 25 (Reporter Li Ping) At 12:20 on July 25, more than 200 Shanghai tourists who took the D771 train successfully arrived in Lanxi City, Zhejiang Province, which is also the first cross-provincial EMU trade since the Ministry of Culture and Tourism resumed inter-provincial (autonomous regions and cities) on July 14.
It is located in the central and western part of Zhejiang Lanxi City, beautiful scenery, there are many scenic spots such as Zhuge gossip village, underground long river, Zhiyan ancient village, etc. During the two-day and one-night itinerary, more than 200 Shanghai tourists will enjoy these attractions one by one.
Li Li, deputy general manager of Shanghai Railway International Tourism (Group) Co., Ltd., said that in accordance with the latest policy, the company focused on the needs of cross-provincial travel, the first time to communicate with Lanxi City, carefully launched "Shanghai to Lanxi" and "summer reward two-day tour" products, products launched less than a week to sell out.
Aunt Sun, from Shanghai, said that she had not gone out this year because of the epidemic.
"At home for a long time, as soon as I saw a team tour, I immediately shared the news with my friends to sign up, I have never been to Lanxi before, and I am very much looking forward to this trip," Aunt Sun said.
It is understood that in September last year, Lanxi City and Shanghai Railway International Tourism (Group) Co., Ltd. signed a strategic cooperation agreement on the project of "taking high-speed rail · Yulanxi" project, and plans to open 12 high-speed rail tourism trains to Lanxi within one year.
