U.S. White House adviser "anti-bite" states to return to work prematurely
On July 23, local time, the number of confirmed cases of new crown pneumonia in the United States exceeded 4 million, accounting for 30% of global cases.
Over the past few months, U.S. President Trump has repeatedly asked all states in the country to return to work and return to school, until recently to change their attitudes and take the initiative to wear masks in public, and his advisers are "responsibly biting" and saying that some state governments have returned to work prematurely.
On the 22nd, the White House presidential adviser, Kellyanne Conway, said at a news conference that some state governments did not comply with the return to work standards and restarted places such as bars prematurely.
Conway also mentioned that the previous claim that the president has "absolute power" to decide on the resumption of work in the states is a false rumor.
“The president is a federalist, and he believes that all states have autonomy.”
She defended Trump.
However, Conway's "rumors" were said by Trump himself at the White House epidemic briefing on April 13.
The self-playing operation of this was ridiculed by netizens as “rewriting history”.
Kylian Conway wants to rewrite history, she’s a liar.
Trump called Michigan Gov. Gretchen Whitmer a dictator because she followed medical guidelines and insisted on a shutdown.
Trump wants to push for a return to work so he can hold rallies.
This isn’t the first time Kylian Conway has caused controversy.
On April 15, Conway blurted out in an interview with Fox News: "It's COVID-19, it's not COVID-1, friends!"
She seems to understand the "19" as a version number, and is ridiculed by netizens: look at the newspaper without common sense!
3-year-old children's college playground was smashed, after receiving compensation and then sued the school is right?
2020-07-26 05:01:11 Source: Legal Daily Author:Wang Sisuo Responsibility Editor:Wang Sisuo
The playground was smashed, and the children received compensation and sued the school.
□ The newspaper's correspondent Zhao Yifan
Three-year-old Xiao Wen was playing in a university playground when he was accidentally smashed into the head by Chen of the softball team while pitching.
After Chen's compensation, Xiaowen's father, Mr. Wen, as Xiaowen's legal representative, brought the school to the court, demanding an apology at the school where the incident occurred, and paying medical expenses, moral damage soothing money, etc., for a total of 20,000 yuan.
Recently, the Beijing Haidian District People's Court after the trial of the case that the school set up a protective network in the playground at the time of the incident, has fulfilled the appropriate safety and security obligations, and Chen has made compensation, according to which the judgment rejected the plaintiff's claim.
Mr. Wen claimed that during the summer vacation in 2019, he took Xiao Wen to play in the school playground, which coincided with the training of the softball team on the playground.
In order to avoid the resulting risks, Xiao Wen, Mr. Wen and many other children and parents are active in the safe area designated by the softball team.
However, Chen, a member of the softball team, left his hand while pitching, resulting in softball flying across the net to the above-mentioned safety area and hitting Xiaowen's back brain.
Mr. Wen immediately took Xiaowen to the hospital for treatment and was diagnosed with head trauma.
Mr. Wen believes that the facilities of the school stadium do not comply with the relevant safety regulations and do not effectively manage the team and related facilities.
The fault of the school led to the above-mentioned events, resulting in the huge pain suffered by Xiao Wen's body and mind, and also brought greater suffering to his family, and the school should bear legal responsibility for it.
In this regard, the school argued that the school has set up a protective network on the playground, and posted management regulations, training notices, informed that entering the playground must maintain a safe distance from the training site and remind itself of their own safety, the plaintiff can not prove that the school "does not meet the safety and security obligations", so they do not agree to compensation.
After the court hearing, it was found that although the school had a safety and security obligation for the management of the playground, although the school had safety and security obligations only needed to meet the general duty of care.
At the time of the incident, the school had set up a protective network on the playground, which had fulfilled its appropriate safety and security obligations, and Chen also compensated Xiaowen for more than two thousand yuan in medical expenses, transportation costs and other losses in accordance with the compensation agreement previously reached, and the two sides agreed to resolve the dispute on a one-time basis.
Afterwards, Xiao Wen's parents once again claimed the school's compensation, which was unfounded, and the court decided to reject all the plaintiff's claims.
After the verdict, neither side appealed, and the sentence has now entered into force.
According to Article 37 of China's Tort Liability Law, as the administrator of a public place, the school has the obligation of safety and security; in the case of damage caused by the behavior of the third party, the third party bears the tort liability, and the manager of the public place who fails to meet the safety and security obligations shall bear the corresponding supplementary liability.
According to the judge, as the manager of a public place, it is most likely to understand the actual situation of the entire place, foresee the possible dangers and damage, so that it is most likely to take the necessary measures to prevent the occurrence of losses or reduce the extent of the damage, and to avoid and mitigate the lowest costs of damage, so the law stipulates that they bear the corresponding security obligations to engage in social activities.
In this case, in this case, for unspecified entrants in playgrounds that are freely available to the public, the security obligations of schools should be commensurate with the social activities they are engaged in, specifically, they should mainly take basic security measures and have the obligation to inform about hidden dangers.
In judicial practice, it is also not appropriate to impose excessive safety and security obligations on managers in public places.
If the school has adopted a protective network and fulfilled the obligation of notification, it can be determined that the school is not at fault and should not bear legal responsibility.
In addition, for third-party infringement, even if the administrators in public places such as schools do not fulfill their safety and security obligations, their responsibility is also as a supplement to damages, according to the newly promulgated civil code, managers bear supplementary responsibilities, can also be recovered to the third party.
Therefore, in such accidents, the victim should no longer expand the scope of the claim after receiving compensation from the direct infringer.
Under the normalization of epidemic prevention and control, people's enthusiasm for sports and fitness is high.
With the gradual liberalization of inter-provincial tourism business, the tourism market is about to usher in a recovery.
Fujian Province has resumed inter-provincial tourism business since July 21st, and in the first weekend after opening up, Xiamen, as a popular tourist destination, ushered in the peak of passenger flow.
As a popular tourist destination city, there are many tourists who arrive in Xiamen on weekends.
Xiamen Railway Station is expected to send 3.7 million passengers, and the passenger flow at the airport is dominated by students, tourism and family visits.
The tourism market has gradually rebounded, and in July, Xiamen Airport operated an average of 440 flights per day, and domestic flights have recovered to 80% before the epidemic.
The airline has encrypted the air express from Xiamen to Shanghai, Beijing, Kunming, Xi'an and other major cities to seize the recovery of the tourism market.
At present, a number of travel agencies in Xiamen have successively launched a number of domestic inter-provincial tourism products in the summer, and the team itinerary is mainly based on outdoor attractions.
In view of the summer passenger peaks in railway stations and airports, relevant units have increased manpower guidance in areas where check-in counters, security checkpoints and other areas are easy to gather, and Fujian has also optimized and upgraded the "eight Min health codes", realized the sharing of health data and mutual recognition with 31 provinces, and promoted the orderly recovery of the tourism market.
Liu Dehua Liu Qingyun can "disassemble" a new spark
"Expertion 2" recently announced that it will be released on December 24th, becoming the first scheduled film of the New Year.
The second part is still the director of Qiu Litao, and Liu Dehua's supervision and starring, with a new story to unfold.
It is reported that the addition of the "nuclear bomb" element in the second part also makes the challenges faced by the bomb disposal experts more difficult, and a few shocking shots in the forecast have been suspended, and the mushroom clouds of the explosion have been engulfed by the fire, and the scene is quite shocking.
Three years ago, by the original team produced the production of "embulcasting experts", won the year's 5th box office champion, and won 7 nominations in the Hong Kong Film Awards, Qiu Litao × Liu Dehua also became the audience's gold medal partner.
"Blossing Expert 2" is also once again looking forward to whether the trump combination can wipe out new sparks.
"Expertion 2" tells a new story: the former bomb disposal expert Pan Jianfeng (Liu Dehua) fainted at the scene of the bombing and was listed as a suspect by the police.
In order to find the truth, he had to ask Dong Zhuowen (Liu Qingyun), a friend who is also a bomb disposal expert, for help.
The female inspector who is eager to solve the case is also Pang Ling (Nini), the ex-girlfriend of Pan Yingfeng, who is also involved in it.
It is still a bomb disposal expert, but from the scheduled preview, you can feel the complexity of Liu Dehua's new role: breaking a leg, wearing prosthetic limbs, while being chased by Liu Qingyun, who is also a bomb disposal expert, while being commanded by his ex-girlfriend Nini.
What is the relationship between the three people, what did Liu Dehua do in Xiangdao Hotel, and what kind of cases he was involved in, and what setbacks he experienced in the career of bomb disposal experts, and all kinds of mysteries are curious.
It is understood that the highlights of the film are the world's landmark buildings in Hong Kong, coupled with the top special effects production team, which brings a realistic visual impact.
(Reporter Nie Qing)
Comprehensive Russian satellite network reported that July 26 is Russian Navy Day, and the main military parade to celebrate Navy Day was held in St. Petersburg and Kronstadt.
Russian President and Supreme Commander-in-Chief of the Armed Forces of the Russian Federation, Vladimir Putin, arrived in Kronstadt to participate in the festivities, where 15 ships and submarines were reviewed.
On July 28, 2019 local time, a grand military parade was held in St. Petersburg, Russia to celebrate the Navy Festival.
According to reports, Putin congratulated naval officers and soldiers on Navy Day, and sailed in a small boat in the Gulf of Finland from next to the ships that were about to participate in the maritime military parade, and then reviewed the reviewed troops at the subjective ceremonial platform.
Putin said that the Russian naval fleet is equipped with the latest types of ships and special equipment, and the level of equipment is constantly improving.
“Russia’s naval fleet has warships equipped with sophisticated weapons, strategic diving cruisers and multi-role submarines, aircraft such as the latest aircraft, unique weapons and special equipment,” Putin said at a Russian Navy Day parade.
On June 24, local time, Russia commemorated the 75th anniversary of the victory of the Great Patriotic War.
He also said that the Russian naval fleet will gain unique advantages through digitalization and effective defensive means.
According to the report, the main naval parade celebrating the Russian Navy Day was held in St. Petersburg and Kronstadt, with a total of 46 ships participating, including the frigate "Admiral Kasatonov", the large anti-submarine ship "Navy Kurakov", as well as large landing ships, small missile ships, frigates, submarines and so on.
Among them, a series of ships were displayed at rest next to the Winter Palace Bridge in St. Petersburg, the most notable of which was Russia's first battleship "Poltava" in the early 18th century.
In order to avoid the spread of the new coronavirus, only local residents and invited guests were able to enter Kronstadt during this year's naval parade.
The last Sunday in July each year is the Day of the Russian Navy.
The founder of the Beijing Philharmonic Choir, Yang Hong, died at the age of 86.
Beijing News (Reporter Liu Zhen) On July 26th, the Beijing Philharmonic Choir issued an obituary, the founder of the Beijing Philharmonic Choir, a famous Chinese conductor, music educator, a lifelong academic member of the Central Conservatory of Music, and a professor of conducting departments, Yang Hongnian, died in Beijing at 13:55 on July 26, 2020, at the age of 86.
Photo taken from the Beijing Philharmonic Choir's official website.
Yang Hong was born in 1934 in Nanjing, Jiangsu, and loved music since childhood.
In 1951, he was the conductor of Nanjing People's Radio Choir, and in the autumn of 1951, he was admitted to the music department of East China Normal University in Shanghai, where he studied with Professor Yang Jiaren and the German conductor Shizmann, and learned the style and tucology from the former Soviet expert Arzamanov.
In 1958, he taught in the music department of the Beijing Academy of Arts and Teachers, and in 1973, he was transferred to the composition and conductor department of the Central Conservatory of Music.
Yang founded the Beijing Philharmonic Choir in 1983.
For more than 30 years, adhering to the purpose of "love and dedication", he led this choir singing all over the world, and won dozens of awards in important competitions at home and abroad.
It has conducted performances of more than 30 groups such as the choir of the Central Orchestra, the Central Ethnic Song and Dance Troupe, the Oriental Song and Dance Troupe, and the Shanghai Choir, and held a number of symphony concerts and choral concerts.
His works include "Band Training", "Choral Training", "Two Song Writings", "Children's Song Collections" (upper volume) and papers "On Chorus Sound Problems", "On the Sound-level Layout of Orchestra", as well as Translating "Choral Arrangement Law" and "The Harmonic Language of Debussy".
China News Network Chongqing July 26 (Reporter Liu Xian) The Chongqing Municipal Development and Reform Commission issued a message on the 26th that the city has so far retired 4,404 fishermen, accounting for 42.54% of all fishermen.
In an interview with China News Network, 53-year-old Li Daiguo said in an interview with the China News Network reporter that his grandparents were fishing in the Longxi River, followed his father to fish at the age of 11, shook the boat, walked along the Longxi River, went up to Liang Ping in Chongqing, went down to longevity, every time he left home for ten and a half months, relying on fishing to maintain his family's life.
However, since 1997, as the rural population has gradually flocked to the town, there have been more and more residents in Gao'an Town, and the environmental pollution caused has become more and more serious.
Along the Longxi River, paper mills, chemical factories and farms have been built, which have also polluted the river water.
By 2007 and 2008, the Longxi River had turned into stinking ditches.
"The fish scales caught are all black, and they are also black after they are opened."
Li Daiguo said that it is becoming more and more difficult to fish after the river is polluted.
Local efforts have begun to control the pollution of the Longxi River, including clearing, patrolling the river, aquatic resources management and so on.
Li Daiguo also retreated from the fishermen to transfer production and became a member of the river patrol team, taking care of aquatic resources.
Starting from January 1, 2020, the Chongqing Aquatic Biological Protected Area and the relevant waters of the main urban area have been completely banned.
According to the data of the Chongqing Municipal Development and Reform Commission, as of now, Chongqing has recaptured 3,403 fishing vessels and 4,643 fishing vessels that have signed withdrawal agreements, accounting for 63.3% and 86.3% of the three-year total tasks, respectively.
4,404 recaptured fishermen, accounting for 42.54 per cent of all fishermen.
4,404 people have been recaptured, and 4,267 people have been employed, accounting for 96.89 per cent of the recaptured fishermen.
Pension insurance covers 2,691 people, accounting for 61.10 per cent of returning fishermen.
In the next step, Chongqing City will carry out in-depth special rectification actions, accelerate the clean-up and rectification of the Yangtze River's trunk and shoreline utilization projects, complete a new round of Yangtze into the Yangtze River sewage outlet census and carry out the corresponding rectification action, basically complete the "three phosphorus" (referring to phosphorus, phosphorus chemical and phosphorus gypsum) rectification tasks, small hydropower clean-up and rectification work, promote on both sides of the Yangtze River.
Israel strengthens repeated prevention and control of the epidemic
2020-07-26 04:56:44 Source: Guangming Daily Author:Wang Sisuo Responsibility Editor:Wang Sisuo
Israel strengthens repeated prevention and control of the epidemic
At the beginning of the outbreak of the new crown pneumonia epidemic, Israel's prevention and control measures have achieved remarkable results.
However, with the gradual lifting of the ban on prevention and control measures, the number of confirmed cases of new crown pneumonia in Israel has recently increased significantly, and the Israeli government has repeatedly taken emergency measures to strengthen the prevention and control of the epidemic.
On February 28, the first case of new crown pneumonia was confirmed in Israel, in order to quickly close all ports of entry and exit, suspend non-essential industries, change schools to online classes, restrict public transportation and non-necessary social activities, lock down cities with severe epidemics, and jointly maintain prevention and control measures by military and police.
This series of measures quickly achieved positive results, and by mid-May, the number of new confirmed cases of new crown pneumonia in Israel fell back to single digits.
With the control of the epidemic, Israel's various prevention and control measures have been completely unsealed, and since June, the number of new diagnoses of new crown pneumonia has gradually rebounded.
Especially after entering July, the spread of the epidemic has been accelerating.
In recent days, there have been more than 1,500 new daily cases in Israel for 8 days, and as of July 25, 916 new cases were reported on the same day.
As of July 25, there had been 59,745 confirmed cases and 448 deaths in Israel.
Faced with the rapid rebound of the epidemic, the Israeli government has repeatedly taken emergency measures to strengthen the prevention and control of the epidemic.
On July 6, after the number of confirmed cases exceeded 30,000, the Israeli government closed public entertainment venues such as gymnasiums, swimming pools, bars and nightclubs, and introduced a policy of restricting public transportation, stipulating that the number of passengers per bus should not exceed 20.
On the 17th, the government announced a series of new restrictions, including the implementation of "closed cities" over the weekend, and stipulated the implementation of the "closed city" from 17:00 every Friday to 5 o'clock every Sunday.
During this period, people can go out, but places such as shops, shopping malls, barbershops, beauty salons, libraries, zoos, museums, exhibition halls, swimming pools and tourist attractions will be closed, while basic services such as supermarkets and pharmacies will remain open.
At the same time, in all dates and periods, gatherings of more than 10 people are prohibited, gyms, studios and other places will be closed, restaurants and cafes are prohibited, and only takeaway services are allowed.
At the same time, the Israeli people did not pay enough attention to the severity of the epidemic and failed to work with the government in fighting the epidemic.
After the recurrence of the epidemic in Israel, many people took to the streets to protest because of the government's prevention and control measures affecting their own economic interests.
On July 11, tens of thousands of people held demonstrations in Tel Aviv, arguing that anti-epidemic policies affected the economy.
On the evening of the 21st, thousands of protesters gathered in front of Prime Minister Netanyahu's residence in Jerusalem to protest against Prime Minister Netanyahu's promulgation of prevention and control measures such as banning restaurants and cafes without giving corresponding compensation.
In addition, many people in the outdoor activities did not comply with the wearing of masks, to maintain two meters of safe social distance and other regulations, in order to avoid not wearing masks by the police fines, many people only wear masks on the chin or hanging on their wrists.
During the repeated period of the epidemic, the school was the hardest hit by the spread of the new coronavirus, and according to the reporter's recent visit to this kindergarten, the kindergarten teachers and students did not wear masks according to the requirements of the government, and did not maintain a safe social distance of two meters from each other, burying hidden dangers for a large number of teachers and students infected with the virus.
Professor Elly Waxman, a member of the Israeli National Security Council's expert advisory group on combating the epidemic, believes that Israel is moving towards a "dangerous situation", pointing out that Israel's current epidemic prevention and control measures are not enough, and all leisure, entertainment venues and summer schools should be closed to control the further spread of the epidemic.
Waxman said that Israel lacks the overall plan to fight the epidemic, and the parliament and government departments should abandon their interests as soon as possible, reach an agreement on the issue of fighting the epidemic, and formulate clear steps that include relevant restrictions in different departments.
Tel Aviv, July 25, this newspaper's reporter in Tel Aviv
Ningxia Guyuan farmer Wu Fengfang but his wife Dai Tianfu, two people sitting in the car, from 20 miles away from home, rushed to Liangyun cultural compound.
Despite the inconvenient legs of these two years, 77-year-old Dai Tianfu is still looking forward to "coming here after three forks and five times and playing tricks."
This is an inconspicuous yard in the original prefecture of Guyuan City, and unlike the general farmhouse, there are often melodious Qin cavities in the yard, as well as wonderful shadow plays, embroidery works, traditional Qin cavities, eyebrows and so on.
The owner of the compound was named Liang Yun, who had been a carpenter.
More than 10 years ago, he began to plan the construction of a cultural compound.
With the Liangyun Cultural Complex, the cultural life of the villagers has become rich and colorful.
The reporter has not yet entered Liangyun Cultural College, Qin cavity tunes have been passed out.
It is for the villagers to sing Qin cavity selection section is the neighbourly village villagers Bai Lixiang.
She has loved Qin cavity since she was a child, and now has a little fame in the local area, and as long as she has free time, she will come to the cultural compound to perform programs for the villagers.
Recently, Bai Lixiang has also played a live webcast.
Bai Lixiang said: "There is a stage for more people to see their own performances, it is a very happy thing."
On the stage, the singer took a look at it, and the player tuned, although he was an amateur, but his enthusiasm did not diminish.
Just like the rustic style of the farmhouse, in addition to the Qin cavity, the "grassroots" art and non-heritage culture in Liangyun's cultural compound rushed to the surface.
The compound has also collected more than 300 physical objects such as agricultural utensils from different eras, traditional and hand-crafted tiles, paper cuttings, embroidery, and shadows.
Liang Yun led the reporter into the exhibition hall in the courtyard, which showed his collection of old objects, old wine pots, three strings, spinning cars and so on.
Why did an ordinary farmer build a cultural compound?
“The shadow play is my family craft, and I’ve been learning it since I was 15.”
Liangyun Cultural Building was established in 2012, becoming the first rural "intangible cultural heritage exhibition hall" in Ningxia, and it is also a demonstration compound for the protection of intangible cultural heritage in Guyuan City.
In addition to the Liangyun Cultural Complex, more than 120 cultural courtyards and 79 non-governmental performance groups have sprung up in Guyuan City. Among them, there are more than 50 cultural courtyards with a certain scale, such as Shenjiahe Cultural College, Wang Yonghong Cultural Academy, Yang Lang Cultural College, etc., covering all townships and streets in Yuanzhou District, with more than 5,000 participants.
These grass-roots artists are active in the field, enriching the cultural life of the masses and meeting their spiritual needs.
“As life gets better and better, traditional culture can’t just be left behind.”
"Liu's spy war drama" once again returned to "Winning" to see Liu Yunlong Li Liqun's opponent "Strength"-Xinhua.com
The 40-episode spy war drama "Winning" will land on Beijing Satellite TV from July 16.
Based on the true historical facts, "Succite" is based on Soviet military archives that have been sealed for many years and were first introduced.
Liu Yunlong, an actor known to the audience as a "spy war drama", broke through the image in the play and challenged a happy "stuttering agent".
In recent years, the popularity of dramas such as "disguist", "mask" and "kite" has proved the strong vitality of espionage types of dramas.
Different from the previous espionage works, "Winning" looked around the world and extended the background of the story to the battlefield of the Soviet Far East.
Set against the backdrop of the final phase of the Anti-Japanese War in 1944, it tells the story of Tang Fei (Liu Yunlong), a CCP secret intelligence worker, under the leadership of the Secretary of the Linhe Provincial Party Committee of the Chinese Underground Party and the director of the Soviet Far Eastern Intelligence Bureau, to carry out the "Mudan-Ula" strategy of the Soviet Far Eastern Intelligence.
In many espionage dramas, as a high-level spy, the male protagonist is the perfect image of handsomeness, high intelligence, and maturity.
However, in Liu Yunlong's view, such a person is not suitable for spying, "spies should be the kind of people who can't find them at all, if you play out, it's the kind of very handsome image, I want everyone to pay attention to you, you can still lurk?
Therefore, in "Wisting", Liu Yunlong ingeniously designed Tang Fei, the protagonist of his role, as a "stuttering agent" with joy.
The other camp in "Summit" is supported by Fukuhara, a Japanese Fukuhara, played by Liang Guanhua, and Fang Shibao, the director of the police department of Li Liqun.
One South, one north, two powerful drama bones, for the whole play to add a lot of master's attention points.
The director Yin Fei uses the term "shorting drama" to describe Li Liqun and Liu Yunlong's opponent in the play, "absolutely drama, they are particularly tacit understanding, and this tacit understanding of their body is very impactful for me. Many times their plays are 'hanging now', for example, we only wrote the length of half a piece of paper, and I didn't stop when filming, and they would be able to continue."
The masters don't rob each other's plays, the director doesn't stir the play, and when the actors are among the characters to ensure their character status, they can not only shape the characters from the point of view of the characters, but also give the audience more viewing possibilities.
In the play, you can also see a lot of familiar faces in the "Liu's espionage drama", "Kite" was famous for a while, "Mountain City F4", also gathered in "Winning" also gathered three people.
Hou Yu and Liu Mingyang, who played Song Xiao'an and Zhao, once again played Tang Fei's left and right arms.
Director Yin Fei said, "There is no inferiority in these two people, they are only in that era, in that environment with the flow."
Liu Yunlong also took the initiative, "We want to be human. This person's affection means that the people around me must have good and bad, bad people are enemies, but we also have to develop them, and our team must also grow up."
The ending of these two people in the play is also carefully designed by Liu Yunlong, and he believes that he will give the audience a satisfactory answer.
(Reporter Qiu Wei)
Inner Mongolia Arong flag 4 students drowned official: the incident sounded the alarm
On the evening of July 25, the reporter learned from the government of Arongqi in Hulunbuir, Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region, that four local students died due to drowning.
At 15:50 on July 24, 110 of the Arongqi Public Security Bureau received an alarm saying that there were 6 junior high school students drowning in the area.
After receiving the police, the local police rushed to the scene for the first time, rescued 2 students on the spot, and then the local emergency bureau, water conservancy bureau and other units rushed to the scene, the whole process to participate in the rescue.
According to reports, the rescue site dispatched more than 80 people such as public security police, police, fire, medical care, etc., dispatched three rubber boats to continue to salvage the surrounding waters, and hired professional rescue teams to arrive at the scene, and conducted underwater searches through sonar detection.
The reporter learned that the local rescuers found the first deceased student at 6:40 on July 25, found the second student at 11:30 on the 25th, found the third deceased student at 12:40 on the 25th, and found that the last student was killed at 13:34 on the 25th.
According to officials, this drowning incident has sounded the alarm for the whole society.
At present, the relevant departments of the local government are sorting out some knowledge to prevent drowning, hoping that the tragedy will not happen again.
HONG KONG, July 25 (Xinhua) -- The Secretary for Financial Affairs and Treasury of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) said that Hong Kong's financial market is still active and functioning in an orderly manner.
He expressed optimism about Hong Kong's financial stability and economy.
Xu Zhengyu said at an online seminar co-organized by the Hong Kong Economic and Trade Office in Toronto and the Hong Kong-Canada Chamber of Commerce (Canadian Federation) on the 24th (Toronto time) that Hong Kong is going through a difficult situation because of the "reform storm" and the new crown pneumonia epidemic.
The Hong Kong dollar exchange rate is stable and is biased towards the level of strong exchange guarantees.
There are no clear signs of money outflows from the banking system; instead, more than $11 billion has been flowing in since June.
The bank’s total deposits have also continued to increase in the past few months, and there has been a series of public offerings in the stock market, and market transactions have repeatedly risen.
Xu Zhengyu said that the new crown pneumonia epidemic has put pressure on the global economy and financial markets, but Hong Kong's basic advantages remain unchanged.
Hong Kong’s advantages, including geography, rule of law, high-speed communications, the free flow of information and money, and a simple and low-tax system, continue to make Hong Kong a leading international financial centre.
Xu Zhengyu pointed out that the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region government has set aside HK$6 billion in the Anti-epidemic Fund, creating about 30,000 time-bound positions in the public and private sectors in the next two years, covering people with different skills and academic qualifications.
In order to support the development of financial technology, the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government has also launched the Thousand Talents Scheme to fund local financial technology companies, start-ups and other companies with fintech-related businesses to create 1,000 new jobs, hire local talents and enrich Hong Kong’s fintech talent pool.
Looking to the future, Xu Zhengyu is optimistic about Hong Kong's financial stability and economy.
He encourages Canadian companies to take advantage of Hong Kong’s strengths and its position as an international financial center, an international asset and wealth management center, and a global offshore RMB business hub to develop and invest in the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area and nearby regions.
Lancet article praised China's anti-epidemic efforts and encouraged countries to learn from their experiences
As a country with a population of 1.4 billion, similar in size to Europe or the United States, China's new crown epidemic has been effectively controlled at this stage, and there has been no large-scale transmission, which has largely controlled the domestic epidemic.
The article said that in the past more than a decade, China has made a lot of investment in domestic research and public health construction, which makes China's preparation for the new crown is much better than the preparation of severe acute respiratory syndrome (SARS).
According to the authors, at the time of the SARS outbreak in 2002, China was initially ill-prepared, especially the pathogen could not be determined.
When the new coronavirus was discovered in December 2019, Chinese scientists were soon able to identify the type of virus and shared genome sequencing data internationally on January 11, 2020.
By the end of January, doctors from mainland China and Hong Kong clarified the clinical characteristics of the virus, warning the world about the threat of the new coronavirus through a research paper published in The Lancet.
China has also been at the forefront of vaccine research, under the declaration of a state of emergency, through close domestic cooperation, such research was carried out very quickly and rigorously, and in May and July, respectively, the results of early trials of the new crown vaccine developed in China were announced in The Lancet.
China's experience has shown that it is very important to invest in national health and research systems and to effectively improve laboratory capabilities.
This is the basis for a rapid and effective national response to health emergencies and global health security.
Other countries, especially low- and middle-income countries, are well worth learning.
In addition, China's experience proves that on the basis of strong research, it is necessary for strong high-level and decisive scientific evidence to make correct decisions, so that the new crown epidemic can be effectively controlled.
Governments and their leaders must respect science, understand the values of science, and take action against society in its best interests.
At the beginning of the outbreak, China National Health Construction appointed three groups of infectious disease experts to Wuhan to investigate the risk and transmission of the new coronavirus, and their suggestions provided the basis for Wuhan's "closure" decision on January 23; when some experts put forward the necessity and urgency of building the cabin hospital, the government quickly made a decision and implemented it quickly; at the same time, the extensive participation of the community and the masses also made the epidemic quickly and effectively controlled.
At the end of the article, in responding to the global health emergency, countries need to strengthen global cooperation and joint response.
Journalist Yang Hong
The former inspector of the Wuhai Municipal Party Committee of Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region was expelled from the party
According to the Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region Commission for Discipline Inspection: Recently, with the approval of the Party Committee of the Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region, the Supervision Committee of the Discipline Inspection Commission of the Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region conducted a case review and investigation on the serious violations of discipline by the former inspector of the Wuhai Municipal Party Committee.
After investigation, as a leading cadre of party members, Platinum Hai lost his ideal and belief, for his own self-interest, he blatantly violated the principle of party nature and opposed inspection and rectification; the concept of the organization was indifferent, illegally arranged the transfer of work for others and accepted other people's property in the selection and appointment of cadres; economic greed, illegal business enterprises to obtain huge benefits, engage in power and money transactions, and use power for self-interest; life corruption, resulting in adverse effects.
Pandainhai's serious violations of political discipline, organizational discipline, integrity discipline, and life discipline constitute job violations and are suspected of bribery crimes and embezzlement crimes, and they do not converge after the 18th National Congress of the Party, do not stop, the nature is bad, the circumstances are serious, and they should be dealt with seriously.
In accordance with the relevant provisions of the "Regulations on Disciplinary Measures of the Communist Party of China" and the Supervision Law of the People's Republic of China, after consideration by the meeting of the Standing Committee of the Discipline Inspection Commission of the Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region and submitted to the Party Committee of the Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region for approval, it was decided to give Platinum Hai an expulsion from the Party, adjusting his treatment according to the regulations; collecting his disciplinary and illegal income; transferring his suspected crimes to the procuratorial organs for review and prosecution in accordance with the law.
On the afternoon of the 25th local time, a small plane crashed into the top floor of a multi-storey residential building in Wessel County, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany, killing three people in the accident.
Duisburg prosecutors, the Weiser County Police Department and the Wessel City Fire Department jointly issued a statement on the evening of the same day, saying that at about 14:40 on the same day, a small plane crashed into a house located in the penthouse of a multi-storey residential building in Hyberskamp Street, Weiser County, killing three people.
On the same day, it took off from the city of Malta in the Ruhr district of North Rhine-Westphalia, took off again after docking at the airport in Weiser County, and then crashed into a residential building.
The deceased was identified either as a female occupant in the hit home and two passengers on a small plane.
A two-year-old child in the room was only slightly injured and rescued safely.
The remaining occupants of the house were not injured in the accident, but the mood has not recovered.
According to the footage reported by the German news agency, there was a lot of smoke coming out of the house where the accident occurred, and after firefighters extinguished the fire, they could see that the house was seriously damaged.
At present, the cause of the plane crash is unclear.
The Rheinische Post quoted the police as saying that there were clues that the plane had disintegrated before hitting a residential building.
Police said multiple parts of the crashed plane were found around the scene of the accident.
The German criminal police are working with Duisburg prosecutors and the German Federal Aviation Accident Investigation Bureau to investigate the cause of the accident.
On the same day, the reporter learned from the Chinese Consulate General in Düsseldorf that the museum contacted the local police department and the fire department, and according to the judgment of the scene, there were no Chinese citizens among the casualties.
Singapore's Ministry of Health announced on the 26th that as of 12:00 on the same day, there were 481 new confirmed cases of the new crown in Singapore, with a total of 50,369 confirmed cases and 27 cumulative deaths.
According to the data, among the newly confirmed cases, 5 are local community cases, 4 are imported cases, and the rest are foreign workers living in dedicated dormitories.
Singapore's health ministry said 98% of new confirmed cases were linked to known infections.
There are still 173 new crown patients being treated in hospitals, most of whom are in stable or improved condition and no one is in intensive care.
In addition, 4,648 people were quarantined in community facilities.
Among the newly infected people in Singapore, foreign workers make up the vast majority.
According to statistics, there are 200,000 foreign workers living in 43 dormitories for foreign workers in Singapore, and about 100,000 foreign workers live in other types of dormitories.
Singapore's anti-epidemic interdepartmental working group said recently that the Singapore government is stepping up the testing of special dormitories for foreign workers with a high rate of new crown infections.
After the completion of the testing of all dedicated dormitories, the vast majority of foreign workers will be able to return to work, but they will still have to undergo regular new crown testing.
Dapeng director "auspicious and happy" shortlisted for the Golden Knight Award-Xinhua.com
On July 18, the 23rd Shanghai International Film Festival announced the official list of films selected for the Golden Knight Award.
Dapeng's first real-life theme film "Auspicious" was successfully shortlisted for the Golden Knight Award at this year's film festival, while the film officially released the first poster.
Poster Photo
"Auspicious" of the film is the first real-life theme work directed by Dapeng, and it is also the second relationship with the Golden Knight Award.
The film tells such a story: a comedy film director suddenly wants to return to his hometown in the northeast countryside, hoping to make the family into a literary and artistic film for the New Year, resulting in a series of accidents.
The family members gathered for the film completed the final meeting.
In today's release of the film poster, a member of the family - "three uncles" Wang auspicious sitting in the middle of the picture smoking cigarettes, the background is covered with silver northeastern black land, the prospect is that the Chinese must hang red lanterns on the New Year's Day.
The red lanterns, which symbolize festivities and reunions, have formed a huge contrast with the auspicies of the king, which also seems to reveal the complexity and entanglement in the relationship of this big family.
It is reported that in the film, in addition to the "three uncles" Wang's auspicious daughter played by actor Liu Lu, the rest of the scenes are completed by the real director's family, the film's experimental audio-visual style, breaking the boundaries of drama and reality, giving the audience a new immersive viewing experience.
According to director Dapeng, "auspicious" creation comes from "a providence", a series of sudden changes in the family during filming, so that the original shooting plan had to have to be changed, there is no script of life was finally recorded as a film, but released beyond the design of the tension.
How does the director Dapeng deal with this "givenness", and how can he continue to meet the changes brought about by God's will?
There is no doubt that "Auspicious" is full of experiments, and the lineup and innovative audio-visual style of almost everyone turns the life in front of the camera into a movie, and under the package of real images, the audience will also find the shadow of themselves and their families from the family presented by the film.
NEWS.GOV.MO: Enquiry hotline statistics for the new coronavirus infection response coordination center (July 25, 08H00-July 26 08H00)
From 08H00 on July 25 to 08H00 on July 26, 2020, the inquiry hotline of the novel coronavirus infection response coordination center received a total of 292 telephone inquiries.
Regarding the 291 inquiries about the epidemic, they have been immediately forwarded to the relevant departments for follow-up, as follows:
271 cases of the Health Bureau (involving: inquiries about isolation; inquiries about nucleic acid testing; inquiries between two cards; health codes; others.)
17 cases (involving: enquiring about entry and exit measures; enquiring about the entry and exit measures of Guangdong-Macao vehicles; enquiring about Zhuhai government hotline; enquiring about the stay of documents.)
1 case of the Tourism Bureau (involving: Enquiry about quarantine hotels.)
Education and Youth Bureau 1 (involving: enquiring about how Macao students return to study in the United Kingdom.)
Maritime and Water Affairs Bureau 1 (involving: whether it is necessary to report to the Maritime and Water Bureau and nucleic acid testing related matters if it is required for Hong Kong fishing vessels to enter Hong Kong.)
At the post, Yu Wang and one of the soldiers were on duty.
In this place with an average temperature of less than ten degrees per year, a row of simple barracks stands in the pass, not far from the barracks, a national flag fluttering against the wind, soldiers are on duty in the wind every day, and they need to regularly go to higher-altitude places to patrol.
The warriors climbed the steep slopes of the rocks and needed their hands and feet.
At the end of July, it is when the flowers are luxuriant at low altitudes, and only in the ravines behind the barracks are relatively dense green.
Gao Peng, a warrior who had been stationed at the outpost for six years, pointed to the ravine and said that it was their back garden, and only in July and August of each year to see the grass grow slowly, and soon after, all turned yellow and covered in snow.
Walking patrols can take about nine hours.
In the harsh plateau environment, the soldiers stationed here are accompanied by snowy mountains and glaciers all the year round, and they are also regularly patrolling the higher elevations.
A few days ago, a patrol composed of eight soldiers once again took the patrol road under the leadership of instructor Liang Yixin.
Each soldier weighs about 30 pounds and goes to the target point early in the morning.
On the way, one of the warriors was high and the comrades-in-arms were rescued urgently.
In addition to the patrol mission, the fighters at the Bagupatsukang sentry have to carry out tactical and physical training every day.
The time passes by, the altitude is rising, the oxygen content is getting lower and lower, and the physical strength is constantly overdrawing, which tests the will of the patrol members.
They clenched their teeth, successively crossed several landslide points, and crossed several dangerous beaches.
At about 16 o'clock, it was the lunchtime of the patrols, they took out their own dry food, sat on the ground at an altitude of more than 5,700 meters, accompanied by sleet, and supplemented their physical strength with food.
Soldiers at the Bazhžokang sentry conducted tactical and physical training.
During the rest period, they will play cards together, and the loser will do push-ups, which can be both entertaining and able to exercise physical fitness.
After a short break in the cold wind, they climbed to the target position of this patrol, took out the national flag on the mountain pass, and solemnly swore.
Behind them is the snow-capped mountains, and in front of them are dozens of kilometers of unmanned areas, and they are the safest guardians of the country.
Beijing's consumption season to restart - Xinhua
In accordance with the principle of "comprehensive restart, key planning, orderly promotion, and strict organization", Beijing has restarted various activities in the Beijing consumption season.
On July 26, 1.5 million government and enterprise consumer vouchers were issued, of which 1 million offline catering shopping vouchers and 500,000 smart product vouchers were issued, and consumers could receive them at the Jingdong APP.
Liu Meiying, deputy director of the Beijing Municipal Bureau of Commerce, introduced at the media briefing held on the 25th that the consumption season after the restart will further reduce the allocation of funds for enterprises on the basis of maintaining preferential subsidies for existing consumer coupons.
Starting from the beginning of August, the government and the enterprise's investment at present 1:1 allocation adjustment to 2:1, such as the original consumers to receive a card package to the store after the consumption can enjoy 120 yuan discount, of which the government subsidy of 60 yuan, the enterprise concessions of 60 yuan; adjusted government subsidies of 80 yuan, the profits of enterprises 40 yuan.
During the consumption season, the three major operators will subsidize traffic and terminals around 5G consumption to further promote Beijing's new 5G infrastructure and 5G new consumption.
Chen Maobo pointed out that Hong Kong's economy has been hit by another outbreak due to the epidemic, calling on all walks of life to go through difficult times
HONG KONG, July 26 (Xinhua) -- The Financial Secretary of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government, Chen Maobo, said on the 26th that Hong Kong's positive impact on the new wave of new crown pneumonia epidemic, business exchanges and economic activities have also been hit.
The HKSAR Government reiterates its call on owners of all sizes to reduce rents and work with retailers, restaurants and small and medium-sized enterprises.
On the same day, Chen Maobo published an article entitled "Strong Road to Recovery" on the Internet.
He said that the number of confirmed cases of new crown pneumonia in Hong Kong recently is high, and the situation is grim, affecting people's lives in society and affecting the economy.
When the epidemic is repeated, it is mainly to strictly prevent imported cases, and to deal with and interrupt the chain of transmission of the virus as soon as possible; when the epidemic is controlled, economic activities should be restored accordingly in due course.
He pointed out that in the face of the impact of the new wave of the epidemic, commercial exchanges and economic activities, which had a slight recovery, have also been hit.
For the business community, in addition to the spirit of the contract, social responsibility is equally important, especially for groups that receive large government subsidies in the “guaranteed employment plan”.
He mentioned that Hong Kong's economic situation in the second quarter of this year is still very serious, but the trend of contraction seems to be slightly slower.
In terms of exports, he believes that Hong Kong's peripheral situation is still serious.
Chen Maobo said that Hong Kong's development in the past few decades has shown that every crisis hides new opportunities, and every difficulty hides the key to future development.
Taiwan's eastern waters hit Taiwan's largest earthquake this year
TAIPEI, July 26 (Xinhua) -- At 20:52 on the 26th in the eastern waters of Taiwan, there was a 6.1-magnitude earthquake on the Richter scale, with a maximum magnitude of 4, and the whole Taiwan was felt, which is the largest earthquake in Taiwan this year.
According to Taiwanese media such as Comprehensive Central News Agency, Zhongshi Electronic News, and ETtoday News Cloud, Taiwan's meteorological department reported that the epicenter of the earthquake was 86.5 kilometers southeast of the Yilan county government, that is, the eastern waters of Taiwan, with a depth of 53 kilometers.
China's Seismic Network determined that the earthquake was 5.5-magnitude.
The largest earthquakes in all parts of Taiwan are: Hualien County 4, Yilan County, Taidong County, Nantou County, Yunlin County Level 3, and other counties and cities measured 1 to 2 earthquakes.
Taiwan's meteorological department pointed out that the earthquake is the largest in Taiwan this year, which belongs to the border of the plate, and its epicentres have often experienced earthquakes in the past, and they are also relatively active this year.
In the next week, there will still be aftershocks of more than magnitude 4.
