In the first half of the year, telecommunications network fraud crimes increased by 70%, and the characteristics of the highest inspection summary
According to the highest inspection website news, in the first half of this year, the national procuratorial organs prosecuted a total of 58101 fraud crimes, an increase of 35% year-on-year.
In particular, in the prevention and control of the epidemic, there have been many cases of fraudulent crimes, and the number of procuratorial organs prosecuting fraud crimes accounted for 43.4% of the total number of epidemic prevention and control crimes.
The Supreme People's Procuratorate has carried out targeted guidance, and a total of 9 cases involving fraud have been issued in the tens of typical cases involving epidemic prevention and control.
Judging from the first half of the procuratorial organs' handling of cases, there are many names involved in fraud crimes, from the national macro policies to people's clothing, food and housing, including epidemic-related fraud, "medical support" fraud, "health care products" fraud, "enrollment intermediary" fraud, "routine loan" fraud, defrauding state subsidy fraud, national asset unfrozen fraud, etc.
In particular, some telecommunications network fraud breaks through the restrictions of national borders, regions and people, has the characteristics of stakeholders, cross-border, remote, electronic payment, etc. There are many unspecified victim groups, and the harm is great.
For example, some have set up special companies, rented high-end office buildings, set up multiple departments or positions, used legal online platforms for publicity, recruitment, training and assessment of recruiters, adopted the enterprise operation mode management, wearing a "legitimate cloak", more confusing.
It is the responsibility of the procuratorial organs to punish and prevent crimes in accordance with the law, and to issue early warnings to the public and relevant departments in a timely manner.
In judicial cases, procuratorial organs conscientiously perform their duties, not only insisting on maintaining a high-pressure situation for fraudulent crimes, but also detailing various law enforcement measures, and promoting social governance through the issuance of procuratorial recommendations.
The procuratorial organs strictly control the facts, evidence, procedures and the application of the law in the cases of arrest and prosecution of fraud, on the basis of the facts, based on the law, so as to do nothing.
In particular, for telecommunications network fraud crimes, pay attention to the central role of electronic data in the determination of facts, and strive to build an electronic data, speech evidence, documentary evidence between each other's evidence chain.
For example, if a case of epidemic-related fraud should be handled by the Yinzhou District Procuratorate of Ningbo City, Zhejiang Province, the procuratorial organ intervenes in advance as soon as possible, from the occurrence of the case to the completion, and only takes 5 days, which reflects the attitude and determination to deal with it quickly and rigorously to maintain the overall stability of the society.
In the examination of arrests and prosecutions, pay attention to the pursuit of omissions in cases, correct the omission of 733 people by the public security organs, and correct the omission of the public security organs to review and prosecute 1,113 accomplices.
In the first half of the year, the national procuratorial organs issued 298 procuratorial recommendations for fraud crimes, promoting joint efforts to prevent fraud crimes and promoting in-depth governance.
For example, in response to the loopholes in the supervision of telecommunications networks such as communication enterprises, banks, and intermediary organizations found in the handling of the case, the Guangzhou Procuratorate of Guangdong Province and the Dongguan Municipal Procuratorate made timely procuratorial suggestions, urging relevant units to strengthen supervision, improve mechanisms, and promote the construction of long-term systems.
The fourth is to make every effort to do a good job of recovery.
Local procuratorial organs seize important links such as interrogating investigations to guide evidence collection, review and prosecution, urge investigative organs to actively recover stolen money, cooperate with relevant departments to do a good job in the pursuit of stolen assets, and strive to minimize the economic losses caused by fraudulent crimes to the people.
For example, the Beijing Municipal Procuratorate handled a certain routine loan case, the case involves 22 properties waiting to be seized, in the case that the property may be disposed of in other cases in advance, the creation of a "suspensive execution letter", timely delivery to the relevant courts, it is recommended that the previous seizure of the real estate suspended execution, until the facts of the crime to be determined after the unified disposal, in order to recover the real estate involved, to recover the victim's losses to make the greatest efforts.
The prosecutor reminded everyone that there should be high vigilance against fraud crimes, don't expect to "fall the pie in the sky", and don't think it's cheap to be credulous and keep your "money bag."
Weining County, Guizhou Province: short apple trees wide the road out of poverty-Zhongxin.com
2020-07-26 11:42:58 Source:China Economic Net Author:Zhu Yanjing Responsibility Editor: Zhu Yanjing
In the heat of the summer, the reporter of the Economic Daily-China Economic Network walked into Zhonghai Village in Wening County, Guizhou Province.
In front of the hot sun, villagers Li Yuanzhong hoed grass in the base, although his face was red, but his mouth from time to time humming a few small songs.
Weining County, where the town is located, due to low latitudes, high altitudes, sufficient illumination, large temperature difference between day and night, the output of apples with high sugar content, good taste, in the surrounding area has a certain popularity, but also because of the small head, more spots, has not been able to sell a good price, failed to form an industrial scale.
It used to be a poor township of "Baogu Yangtao Spring and Autumn", and the incidence of local poverty was as high as 25.8% 10 years ago.
In the critical period of poverty alleviation and decisive victory, it is urgent to change traditional planting habits, adjust the industrial structure, and increase the income of farmers.
Chen Chao, secretary of the party committee and a group of people in the town after many visits, believed that the development of the industry can no longer take the old road.
To this end, the town introduced leading enterprises and cultivated apples in a modern way.
Hou Jianwen, deputy general manager of Weining Beyond Agriculture Co., Ltd., came from Shaanxi to the town in 2015, took a look at the local planting conditions, and began to plant apple trees locally from 2016.
At first, the village mobilized Li Yuanzhong to transfer the land out to plant apple trees, and Li Yuanzhong and his wife muttered in their hearts: "For so many years of apples, I did not see who planted apples in the village to make a fortune."
"The apples that are grown are all dwarf apples and won't make apple trees grow too high."
What Li Yuanzhong didn't expect is that this apple planting adopts a new method, the irrigation water pipe is laid under each apple tree, the water and fertilizer are poured to the root of the tree together, and when the fruit is collected in autumn, the tractor drives directly into the orchard, and can pick the fruit while standing.
At present, the apple base has gradually entered the productive period, and the market is also as Hou Jianwen envisioned, Apple is not worried about selling, which is loved by consumers in Beijing, Shanghai, Guangzhou and other cities.
The growing apple industry has made new changes in Li Yuanzhong's life, although it is still planting land, but there is a new source of income.
Li Yuanzhong family has more than 9 acres of land transferred to the apple base, in addition to the guaranteed land transfer fee every year, there are profit dividends after hanging fruit, the husband and wife usually work in the base, "one person can get 80 yuan a day, there are jobs all year round."
Li Yuanzhong told reporters that last year's profit dividends got more than 2,800 yuan, coupled with land transfer fees and the husband and wife's migrant income, an income of more than 80,000 yuan, "eating and wearing, a well-off life has lived."
"At present, it has begun to achieve results, and the annual output value of an acre apple is more than 15,000 yuan, which is about 10 times that of planting corn."
Chen Chao told reporters that the whole town currently planted 20,000 acres of apples, only in Zhonghai Village has 6000 acres, covering 4,056 households, 17,200 people, which covers 656 poor households and 2,952 people, paid more than 6 million yuan a year, and truly realized that the base was built at the door, and there was no need to go out.
Li Yuanzhong, whose pockets are growing up, has also begun to fulfill his "wish".
This year's Lunar Spring Festival, Li Yuanzhong bought an off-road vehicle, and now driving a car to and from work every day, "there are more than a dozen acres of land at home, such as the next step to expand the size of the apple base, all transferred to them, the income will be more."
Economic Daily-China Economic Net reporter Wu Bingze 牛瑾 Wang Xinwei
Membrane separation technology to help crack the "greenhouse effect"-Zhongxin.com
Membrane separation technology to help crack the "greenhouse effect"
New hybrid matrix film preparation technology diagram
A few days ago, Tianjin University's atmospheric environment and bioenergy team made significant progress against "membrane separation to capture carbon dioxide" and successfully developed a new hybrid matrix film preparation technology to greatly improve the carbon dioxide capture performance of membrane materials.
The results have been published as a cover article in the international journal “Greenhouse Gases: Science and Technology”.
The "greenhouse effect" is a major environmental problem plaguing human development, and carbon dioxide emissions are responsible for the "greenhouse effect".
How to efficiently capture and use carbon dioxide emitted by humans is the focus of scientists.
The "membrane separation method" is an emerging carbon dioxide capture technology, which separates carbon dioxide gases with the help of membrane materials, which has the characteristics of high efficiency and energy saving and simple operation.
How to make the membrane material "deep breathing" and improve the efficiency of gas separation is the difficulty of trapping carbon dioxide using the membrane separation method.
The scientific research team of Tianjin University innovated ideas and explored the impact of different solvents on the separation performance of membrane gases through repeated experiments.
The results of the experiment show that with N-methylpyropyrolidone as the preparation solvent, the distribution of carbon nanotubes in the generated membrane material is more uniform and "more breathable", which effectively improves the gas separation efficiency and rate of the membrane material.
With this new technology to prepare the mixed matrix membrane, the carbon dioxide separation performance is close to the current theoretical separation limit of such membrane materials.
“New technology provides new ideas for membrane separation to capture carbon dioxide.”
Li Run, a member of Tianjin University's atmospheric environment and bioenergy team, said: "We hope that this technology can provide strong support for future coal-fired power plants and chemical enterprises to deal with flue gas, and play a major role in controlling greenhouse gas emissions and other fields."
Before voluntarily filling in the report, first understand what is the professional level difference-Zhongxin.com
2020-07-27 02:22:36 Source:Chongqing Morning News Author: Yuxiao Responsibilities Editor: Yuxiao
Before volunteering, you need to find out what is a professional difference.
Every year to fill in the college entrance examination volunteers, there are students or parents because they do not understand the words involved in the voluntary report, and then affect the voluntary filling.
This year, five colleges and universities of Beijing Jiaotong University, Beijing University of Science and Technology, Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications, Beijing Forestry University and Beijing University of Chemical Technology jointly released their 2020 enrollment policies and cancelled their professional-level differences.
What is the meaning of professional grade difference, and what is the significance in volunteer reporting?
There are three types of professional allocation rules.
Experts remind that before filling in the volunteer, we must read the enrollment charter of the favorite school, and understand the admission rules of colleges and universities, including the proportion of transfers and the rules of professional distribution.
Professional allocation rules, refers to after the transfer of colleges and universities, there are mainly three ways of professional priority, score priority, and professional grade difference for professional admission.
The specific method used by the university will be clarified in the Admissions Charter.
However, there are also some colleges and universities where the principle of admission is that the total score is preferred, and there is no grade difference between the majors.
That is to say, candidates will queue according to the total score, when the score does not reach the first professional voluntary admission score line, it will see whether it has reached the second professional voluntary admission score line, and so on until the admission to the last professional volunteer, there is no grade difference between professional volunteers.
The so-called "professional grade difference" is that when the college arranges the candidate's profession, according to one or more points published in the enrollment charter, it is necessary to determine the admission of different professional volunteer candidates, and this score value is "professional grade difference".
That is to say, the difference between the scores of the first professional volunteers and non-first professional volunteers of the college in the admission of candidates, and the difference between the grades of professional volunteers, such as 3 points, 2 points, 1 points and so on.
For example.
Assuming that the student Xiaoming applied to A university and scored 560 points, his professional volunteers were: computers, international trade, automation, mechanical engineering, e-commerce, and the professional admission of A colleges and universities to implement a professional-level approach, which is divided into 2 points, 1 points, 1 points, and 0 points.
In terms of professional allocation, if Xiaoming's first professional volunteer meets the professional admission requirements and the professional has a planned balance, then Xiaoming is admitted to the "computer" major; if the computer is not admitted, his score will be subtracted by 2 points, according to 558 points, according to the first professional volunteer to apply for "international trade", to determine whether it meets the professional admission conditions; if it is still unable to meet the professional admission conditions, the score is subtracted by 1 (i.
Different universities have different professional grade settings.
With the popularization of parallel volunteers, many colleges and universities have now cancelled the professional grade difference, but this year there are still some colleges and universities have retained this method, from the "enrollment charter" published by each school, this year there are mainly more than 20 universities set up professional grade difference.
For example, Sichuan Agricultural University, Shandong University of Science and Technology, Heilongjiang University of Traditional Chinese Medicine, Jiangsu University of Science and Technology, Jiangxi Normal University, Chengdu Medical College, Northeast Electric Power University, Jimei University, Nanjing Medical University, Nanjing University of Technology, Ningxia University, Shandong University of Technology, China Civil Aviation Flight College and so on.
In these colleges and universities, the professional grade difference set by each university is different.
Some colleges and universities in each major have a grade difference, such as Ningxia University, the file has been cast into the school candidates, according to the order of candidates to fill in the professional volunteers after the reduction of 1 points after the ranking of admission.
And there are universities between different majors, set up different professional grade differences.
For example, Jimei University, the total difference between professional volunteers is 4 points, that is, the difference between the first professional volunteer and other professional volunteers is 3 points, there is no grade difference between other professional volunteers, which is regarded as parallel volunteers, and the difference between other professional volunteers and professional volunteers is 1 points.
When filling in the volunteer, candidates and parents must carefully read the admission policy of the submitted school, to see if there is a poor professional level, what is the form of poor grade, in full consideration of the score at the same time, but also a reasonable analysis of the proposed schools and majors, if the college in the admissions charter clearly adopts the grade difference mode of admission, candidates in the choice of professional, pay attention to the gradient between each major, improve the admission rate.
Zhongqing Morning News · Upstream Journalist Lin Qi
This year's first Atlantic hurricane made landfall in Texas, which was hit hard by the epidemic.
The U.S. National Hurricane Center announced early in the morning that Hurricane Hanna had reached speeds of 145 kilometers per hour, which is expected to cause heavy rainfall in southern Texas and northeastern Mexico until next Monday, and the rain will cause rapid flooding.
At present, with the gradual advancement to the land, customs have weakened, and although there are power outages in local areas, there are no statistical reports of casualties for the time being.
Some local officials in Texas are preparing to deal with a tornado that is likely to occur along the coast.
President Donald Trump said on Twitter that his office was closely monitoring the dynamics of Hurricane Hannah and Hawaii's Douglas, and called on the public to listen to the local government's emergency management information to protect families and property.
At the same time, the new crown epidemic in Texas is also deteriorating sharply, and the number of infections is soaring, with more than 390,000 confirmed infections and more than 5,000 deaths.
When this hurricane strikes, the government will face the dual problem of accommodating the homeless while preventing the epidemic from worsening again.
The establishment of a special committee for the first time, the collective signing of the "long contract" The 3rd Expo exhibitors alliance to build a "integration link"-Xinhua.com
On July 26, the first meeting of the 3rd CIIE Exhibitor Alliance was filmed in Shanghai.
Xinhua News Agency, Shanghai, July 26 (Reporter Zhou Rui) 26th, the 3rd Import Expo Exhibitor Alliance set up a professional committee for the first time here, the first batch of special committees set up, including the public health and epidemic prevention committee and the Dairy Committee, 35 member companies also signed a three-year long-term exhibition memorandum of cooperation, the Expo Exhibitor Alliance's role continues to strengthen.
At the first meeting of the 3rd CIIE Exhibitor Alliance held here on the 26th, a number of exhibiting alliance member companies such as South Korea Hyundai, the United States Dow Chemical, Japan Shiseido, New Zealand New Zealand, German Siemens, French Michelin and AstraZeneca signed a three-year long-term exhibition cooperation memorandum, and revised and perfected the alliance charter was also announced for the first time.
On July 26, the ceremony of the establishment ceremony of the Dairy Professional Committee photographed in Shanghai.
According to the latest regulations, the exhibition will introduce the rotation mechanism of the lead unit and strengthen the function of the special committee.
The special committee will make suggestions for the analysis of the development trend of the industry and promote the sustainable development of the industry.
At the same time, the integration of the entire industrial chain resources of the industry, with large and small, drive related enterprises to participate in the exhibition, and build the Expo into a high ground for industry enterprises.
The establishment of a public health epidemic prevention committee for the first time is particularly important for the current fight against the new crown pneumonia epidemic.
As the vice president unit of the 3rd CIIE Public Health Epidemic Prevention Committee, Qiu Jianping, general manager of Abbott's rapid diagnosis business in Greater China, said that in the next step, Abbott will work with more industry partners to explore new solutions and cooperation models to help China and the world fight against the new crown pneumonia epidemic.
On July 26, the public health epidemic prevention professional committee held in Shanghai was established at the ceremony.
It is reported that the third Expo for the first time to set up a public health epidemic prevention zone, as of now there are nearly 50 global enterprises registered to participate in the exhibition, the exhibition area of more than 10,000 square meters.
During the first Expo in 2018, the Expo Exhibitor Alliance was established by exhibitors at the initiative of exhibitors, aiming to become a platform for high-quality exhibitors to exchange and cooperate with each other, a platform for linking information and resource sharing among all exhibitors, and a think-tank platform for suggestions and suggestions to promote economic, trade and business exchanges and development between China and other countries (regions) around the world.
Up to now, 142 companies have joined the Exhibitor Alliance, covering 23 countries and regions around the world.
3-year-old girl in Belgium dies from new coronavirus infection
Belgium's health department said on the 24th that a three-year-old girl died of the new coronavirus infection, the country's youngest new coronavirus death.
Belgian health ministry spokesman Budwin Kateri said the girl had had other serious illnesses before she was infected with the new coronavirus; in addition to the girl, an 18-year-old recently died of the new coronavirus infection.
Catri said that 85 per cent of new coronavirus diagnoses in Belgium last week were under the age of 60.
He reminded people who are in good health and at a younger age not to take it lightly.
"Although it is rare for young people to die of new coronavirus infections, no one now has immunity."
Last week, the number of new coronavirus diagnoses in Belgium increased by 89% compared to the previous week, with an average of 2.9 deaths per day from new coronavirus infections, up from an average of 1.7 per day in the previous week.
During the peak of the epidemic in Europe, the proportion of people infected with the new coronavirus in the Belgian population ranked among the best in Europe.
There are more than 11 million people in Belgium.
According to the latest data, 64,847 people have been infected with the new coronavirus in Belgium.
Katri warned earlier this week that people must take action before snowballs get bigger and eventually cause an “avalanche.”
In order to curb the rebound of the epidemic, Belgian Prime Minister Sophie Vermes announced on the 23rd that the relevant provisions of people's wearing masks in public places will be more stringent, and the plan for further lifting of restrictive measures in August will also be suspended.
(Guo Qian) [Xinhua News Agency micro-construction]
Jiangsu adds 1 new case of asymptomatic infection imported from abroad-Zhongxin.com
According to the official Weibo news of the Jiangsu Provincial Health and Health Commission, there were no new confirmed cases in Jiangsu at 0-24 hours on July 25.
As of 24:00 on July 25, 655 confirmed cases have been reported in the province (of which 24 cases have been imported from abroad), all of which have been discharged, except for one confirmed case imported from abroad that has been isolated and treated in designated hospitals.
On the same day, there were 1 new cases of asymptomatic infection imported from abroad.
As of 24:00 on July 25, 4 cases of asymptomatic infected persons who are being centrally isolated and medically managed were imported from abroad.
At present, 14,084 close contacts of confirmed cases and asymptomatic infected persons have been traced in the province, 13,943 people have been relieved of medical observation, and 141 people are still undergoing medical observation.
[Editor: Chen Haifeng]
HONG KONG, July 25 (Xinhua) -- The Secretary for Business and Economic Development of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) said on the 25th that all APEC member economies should act together to jointly fight the epidemic and promote economic recovery, and avoid the establishment of unnecessary trade barriers in accordance with the rights and obligations set by the World Trade Organization.
Qiu Tenghua made the above statement while participating in the video conference of trade ministers to combat the new crown pneumonia epidemic held by the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) on the 25th.
At this meeting, the participating ministers exchanged views on APEC's response to the impact of the new crown pneumonia epidemic, as well as the substantive programs that can be taken to promote economic recovery in the region.
Qiu Tenghua said that the public health and economic crisis triggered by this epidemic has had an unprecedented far-reaching impact on society and economy.
"We are in a double battle, and we must defeat the epidemic before we can save the economy."
We must have a clear goal, the virus is our common enemy, cooperation can win, but only failure.”
Qiu Tenghua said that the series of trade restrictions caused by the new crown pneumonia epidemic did not help to control the epidemic.
Trade is the key solution to the current problem and should not be seen as a problem.
He condemned all discriminatory and divisive policy measures, and urged all economies to keep their borders open at this critical time, keep their supply chains running smoothly, and refrain from erecting trade barriers or adopting irrational trade policies.
414,000 new crown cases confirmed in the U.S., becoming the second most serious state in the U.S.
According to the Johns Hopkins University website in the United States, as of about 8:34 on the 26th of Beijing time, Florida of the United States has reported more than 414,000 confirmed cases of the new crown, surpassing New York's 411,000, becoming the second largest "epidemic area" in the United States after California.
The Florida Department of Health said on the 25th that Florida reported 124 deaths on the 24th.
This is the 10th time since the start of the new coronavirus pandemic that Florida’s number of daily deaths has exceeded 100.
It is reported that the total number of cases in Miami-Dade County, Florida's worst outbreak, has exceeded 100,000.
There are currently 8,974 patients hospitalized with the new coronavirus in Florida, of which 1,874 are in Miami-Dade.
Since July 4, the number of new crown hospitalizations in the state has increased by 79%.
Since the first U.S. state reopened on April 24, 91,000 lives have been taken from the new crown.
According to data provided by Johns Hopkins University, the total number of confirmed cases reported in the United States has reached 4.176 million, with at least 146,000 deaths.
People in Chengdu gathered around the U.S. consulate and police stopped people from "looking too happy."
In response to the U.S. closure of China’s consulate general in Houston, China announced on Friday that it was closing the U.S. consulate in Chengdu.
On Saturday, the U.S. consulate’s insignia was taken down, and on Sunday, a dark-glass car left the consulate in the hustle of passers-by.
On Sunday, many people in Chengdu gathered in front of the U.S. consulate to take pictures, and those who had not been there were also driven to take a look because of the curiosity of current events.
Agence France-Presse Chengdu station reporters also went to the U.S. Consulate in Chengdu to observe some, sent back the news that the curiosity is endless, and there are still many parents with their children to take a walk to see the consulate, take pictures of the building, or take selfies.
The consulate was surrounded by guards, and from time to time, the police were “reconciling” people’s behavior, and they didn’t seem to allow any out-of-the-box behavior: a woman was stopped just getting ready to sing a red song, and a guard confiscated a banner.
However, the residents of a nearby residential building successfully pulled up a huge Chinese flag on his balcony and shouted slogans in support of China.
Opened in 1985, the U.S. Embassy covers all consular-related matters of the United States in southwestern China, especially in the Tibet Autonomous Region.
The Chinese government's response to the U.S. has been relatively restrained: Many Chinese have asked the government to shut down the U.S. consulate in Hong Kong online, but officials have simply said that "closing the U.S. consulate in Chengdu is a necessary and legal response to the unreasonable behavior of the United States."
At present, in addition to Chengdu, the United States also resides in Guangdong in China, in Shanghai, in Shenyang, in Wuhan, in Hong Kong.
Large-scale financial media action "walking the village live to see poverty alleviation" departure - Today's news - Hunan Daily Network - Huasheng Online
Hunan Daily · New Hunan client July 25 (Reporter of this newspaper) July 25th, a large-scale financial media action sponsored by the Central Radio and Television Station Financial Program Center "walking village live to see poverty alleviation" started from Xuzhou, Jiangsu Province, two caravans carrying 5G new media mobile cloud broadcasting system were sent at the scene.
General Secretary Xi Jinping pointed out that "2020 is a landmark year, and we will build a well-off society in an all-round way to achieve the goal of the first century of struggle, and 2020 is also the year of decisive victory in the fight against poverty."
The large-scale financial media action "walking the village to see poverty alleviation" is an important measure for the financial program center of the Central Radio and Television Station to cooperate with this major theme and do a good job in promoting poverty alleviation.
The action will enter more than 20 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities across the country to get rid of poverty, excavate the story of living poverty alleviation, directly hit the dramatic changes in the appearance of the village, and show how the villagers can break through the dilemma of survival and development and go to the road to wealth.
This operation will last for more than three months.
The reporter started from Xuzhou in two ways, all the way to the southwest line, through Anhui, Hubei, Jiangxi, Hunan, Guangxi, Guizhou, Sichuan, Chongqing, Yunnan, Tibet and other places; the other way through the northwest line, through Henan, Shaanxi, Gansu, Qinghai, Xinjiang, Ningxia, Inner Mongolia, Shanxi, Hebei and other places, more than 10,000 kilometers.
In the form of reporting, "walking villages live to see poverty alleviation" bold integration.
The economic development of the caravan to the village will be broadcast through the CCTV financial channel of the Central Radio and Television Station, the voice of the central and broad economy, China traffic broadcasting, and the CCTV financial new media.
Among them, live TV will mainly be completed in the CCTV financial channel's midday news program "the world's finance" (first broadcast time: Monday to Sunday 12:00-13:00), CCTV financial channel's golden news program "economic information broadcast" will open a poverty alleviation reporting column (first broadcast time: from Monday to Sunday 20:30-21:30).
At the same time, the caravan will carry out up to 1-hour live broadcast of each village in the CCTV financial client, and the audience can watch the live broadcast and participate in the sweepstakes by downloading the CCTV financial APP.
In terms of technical application and studio design, "walking the village live to see poverty alleviation" has the courage to break through, creating a "new media caravan in the field".
The car is equipped with 5G new media mobile cloud broadcasting system, using 5G+4K/8K+AI technology to realize the organic combination of online and offline, large-screen and TV broadcast.
Configured with a three-in-one studio area, which is converted from a container, with a length of 12 meters, a width of 2.55 meters, and a height of 3.98 meters, the box adopts a hydraulic automatic expansion structure, which can turn over 120 degrees.
The broadcast area can also be expanded automatically, and the external expansion platform has an area of more than 50 square meters, which can meet the scene requirements of most programs.
At present, Kunming Dongchuan District is already hot in the summer, and what is hotter than the weather is the poverty alleviation workshop next to the relocation and resettlement.
Lu Ling, an employee of Kunming Esford Electronic Technology Co., Ltd., said, "Now, as soon as you go out of the house, you will enter the factory door and make money, thanks to the free vocational skills training organized by trade unions."
Entering the poverty alleviation workshop for the processing of electronic components in Tongdu Street, Dongchuan District, a hot and busy picture came into view.
Lü Ling, who is more than 40 years old, is a single-parent mother, with children alone, but also to take care of elderly parents.
In her most difficult time, the Dongchuan District Federation of Trade Unions helped come up with an idea to find a way to "send charcoal in the snow" before and after running.
Since 2018, Lü Ling has enjoyed assistance policies such as housing, education, social security, and employment, as well as subsidies issued by trade unions at all levels.
This year, her child has successfully graduated and is employed, and she also has a job and income after participating in skills training, and has been released at the end of April.
It is reported that Dongchuan District General Organization to help poverty alleviation special skills training project, is part of the Yunnan Provincial Federation of Trade Union skills training work.
Combined with the characteristics of difficult employees in the poverty alleviation relocation and resettlement sites in the district, in-depth investigation and understanding of training needs, determining the type of training, and planning to train a total of 450 electricians, welders, and noodle pointers in the near future.
Recently, Li Yi, an employee of the Yunnan Menglian County Branch of the Agricultural Bank, wrote a sincere thank you letter to the County Federation of Trade Unions.
In this letter, she sincerely thanked her that between August 2013 and January 2017, the trade union gave her Jinqiu student aid to help her complete her studies.
In 2004, Li Yi's father died in a car accident, and his mother was included in the archives of difficult workers, and since then, he has been enjoying the care of establishing a file card policy.
With the help of local trade unions, Li Yi successfully completed his studies.
Since 2016, 3,809 households have been rescued through institutional guarantees and precise assistance.
The successful relief of the Lu Ling family and Li Yi is a microcosm of the Yunnan trade union's efforts to promote the relief and relief of difficult employees.
According to the staff section of the Legal and Rights Protection Work Department of the Yunnan Provincial Federation of Trade Unions, the province has comprehensively strengthened the dynamic management of the archives of difficult employees, promoted the normalization of filing work, and timely included in the help system for difficult employees who meet the conditions for archiving; broadened the application channels for difficult employees, and used WeChat to open an online application service platform for difficult employees, so as to facilitate the timely active declaration of difficult employees.
During the epidemic period, migrant workers are difficult, in order to help the difficult workers to alleviate the pressure of life, Yunnan Province arranged more than 13 million yuan to send warm funds, in accordance with the national level of difficult workers in the archives of 2000 yuan per household, provincial-level difficult workers per household 1500 yuan standard, more than 6,000 households at the national level and more than 1,000 provincial-level difficult workers in the implementation of special warm condolences activities.
At the same time, all kinds of Internet recruitment platforms such as the province's general and social departments and Zhilian recruitment are docked, the recruitment information will be pushed to difficult employees, and employment consulting, employment guidance and other services will be provided.
